1
00:00:06,965 --> 00:00:10,093
[Dail] You have no idea
how badly I've wanted to come in here.

2
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:12,262
I've wanted to be
in this Dining Room so bad.

3
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:14,806
Dail and I've never been
to the Main Hall before.

4
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,184
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-So this is the Main Hall.

5
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:18,477
Let's do a toast.

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,811
[Ddolddol] Good work.

7
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:25,651
-[Pani Bottle] Ah...
-[slurping loudly, exclaims]

8
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,986
[slurping loudly]

9
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:30,530
Are you going to bed, Horseking?
Are you going to sleep?

10
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,866
-I don't know.
-Okay.

11
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:33,992
Good night.

12
00:00:34,076 --> 00:00:35,160
-See you tomorrow.
-[Horseking] Good night.

13
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:37,663
AWKWARD RESPONSE FROM OTHERS

14
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:39,581
[Ddolddol] I don't think
we're exactly welcome.

15
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:41,750
-Huh?
-I don't think we're exactly welcome.

16
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,795
Even better.
This is exactly what I wanted.

17
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:48,298
They reacted like, "There are
more survivors than I expected."

18
00:00:48,382 --> 00:00:50,300
Like, "Get a load of these punks."

19
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:51,385
I love it.

20
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:53,512
Let's crush them all.

21
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:56,431
When we returned to the house,

22
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,475
there wasn't a single person who said,

23
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:02,938
"I'm glad you guys are back.
Welcome back."

24
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:06,358
EARLIER IN THE MAIN HALL

25
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:08,068
[Pani Bottle groans] My back hurts.

26
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:13,323
STRANGE TENSE MOOD IN THE MAIN HALL

27
00:01:13,407 --> 00:01:15,409
[Ddolddol] I got the feeling
they were thinking,

28
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,411
"They actually made it back alive."

29
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:21,957
That actually gave me
even more motivation.

30
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,251
The three of us have such a strong bond

31
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:27,296
that whenever we say something,
it carries a lot of weight.

32
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:30,549
I think the entire dynamic will change.

33
00:01:31,425 --> 00:01:33,468
Honestly, we had amazing teamwork.

34
00:01:33,594 --> 00:01:35,053
Today went really well.

35
00:01:35,137 --> 00:01:37,931
But I think
we were too brutal when we took them out.

36
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:40,350
-What did you do?
-They couldn't do a thing.

37
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,978
It wasn't because it was Jieun.
We would've taken out anyone.

38
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,355
[Ddolddol] The three of us were already
on the same side.

39
00:01:45,439 --> 00:01:47,107
[Dail] It was basically like this.

40
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,900
Whoever ended up there
would never get out.

41
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:52,821
You might as well have brought
someone strong in,

42
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:55,490
because nobody could beat us.

43
00:01:55,574 --> 00:01:57,576
[Ddolddol] I think going down to prison
was a good thing

44
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:01,246
because I found people
who trusted me and had my back.

45
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:09,087
The prison team came back
with such a strong bond.

46
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:12,674
They were almost like a family.
It was more than an alliance.

47
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:16,678
Our concern is that the Seeker Vote
is coming up tomorrow.

48
00:02:16,762 --> 00:02:18,388
[Pani Bottle] Let's talk about that later.

49
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:20,140
I was going to bring it up anyway.

50
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,100
[Jaegyun] You can talk
about it now. It's fine.

51
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,227
Just in case.

52
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:27,272
[Eunsil] Let's go.

53
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,818
[Sanghyun] I think
they're going to talk about me.

54
00:02:31,902 --> 00:02:33,070
[Junseo] That you're the Seeker?

55
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,113
[Sanghyun] Ddolddol
keeps suspecting me so much.

56
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:37,616
I'm starting to get a little angry.

57
00:02:40,369 --> 00:02:41,953
Did he leave?

58
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:43,038
Yeah. So...

59
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,414
What was Sanghyun's last name?

60
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:45,791
-Youn Sanghyun.
-Youn Sanghyun?

61
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:49,002
-I'm 97 to 99% sure it's him.
-[Pani Bottle] I know.

62
00:02:49,086 --> 00:02:52,464
I've barely spoken to him,
but isn't he clearly winning right now?

63
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:53,548
Yes.

64
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:54,633
He's dominating.

65
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:55,842
-[Ddolddol] He has 120 million won.
-Right.

66
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:59,012
It's about time someone kept him in check.

67
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:02,391
That's what we agreed among ourselves.

68
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:07,229
I heard he found a hidden mission
that wasn't even in the original rules.

69
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:10,232
Are you really taking his word for it?

70
00:03:10,315 --> 00:03:14,653
Because of that,
we're a little suspicious of him.

71
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,822
But I'm not sure if the others
feel the same way.

72
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:18,323
[Dail] Of all people, the one in first?

73
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:22,160
If you're on the fence,
maybe you should team up with us

74
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:25,288
-and split that group up.
-[Ddolddol] Trust my gut on this.

75
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:31,711
Even if Sanghyun isn't the Seeker,
there's a lot to gain.

76
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:36,049
Wouldn't it be good to prove his alibi
if he doesn't want people to suspect him?

77
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:41,304
[Pani Bottle] We came back from prison,
and we're small in number.

78
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:44,141
I thought we needed to bring
more people onto our side.

79
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,685
I suspect Sanghyun is the Seeker.
If he's not, no big deal.

80
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,020
It's because he's so good
and dominating the game.

81
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:51,398
I told them we need to keep
the strong player in check.

82
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:55,360
Give it some thought. We're not saying
we have to stick together forever.

83
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:57,070
Later, we'll split up anyway.

84
00:03:57,154 --> 00:04:00,240
But for now, I think we need
to keep the former cops in check.

85
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:03,660
So yeah, we did talk about that
among ourselves too.

86
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:04,744
We did talk about it.

87
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:07,289
THE PRISON ALLIANCE SUGGESTS
JOINING FORCES WITH THEM

88
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:10,375
[ZZONE] The prison alliance
seems really strong.

89
00:04:10,459 --> 00:04:11,710
[Jimin] Their bond is no joke.

90
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:14,671
The prison team is too intimidating.

91
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:15,964
[ZZONE] They're definitely intimidating.

92
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:18,508
Up until now,
the alliances have always been

93
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:22,220
about teaming up with people
who could benefit you in each match.

94
00:04:22,304 --> 00:04:24,181
But the prison crew is insane.

95
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,309
They're like, "We're going to eliminate
everyone here."

96
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,102
But they have four people over there.

97
00:04:29,186 --> 00:04:31,354
[ZZONE] It's three now since Sujin's gone.

98
00:04:31,438 --> 00:04:33,899
-[Jimin] Right.
-Joonsu is pretty close with them too.

99
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,860
He'll probably side with whoever gives him
the best advantage.

100
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,945
Jaegyun is close with them.

101
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:45,535
To break them apart,
we need to send them back to prison.

102
00:04:46,161 --> 00:04:49,539
[Jimin] From what I heard from the people
who survived prison,

103
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:53,877
it felt like they teamed up
and eliminated Jieun.

104
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:57,589
It felt like it'd naturally turn
into a battle

105
00:04:57,672 --> 00:05:00,842
between the mansion group
and the prison members.

106
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,136
I'm not sure what will happen
going forward.

107
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:10,352
[crow cawing]

108
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,523
[Eunsil] It feels like
we've been here forever,

109
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:16,900
but we've only done the second Main Match.

110
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,693
Only two have been eliminated.

111
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:20,570
We need to eliminate them all quickly,

112
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:22,197
-starting with the prison family.
-[♪ intriguing music playing]

113
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,323
[Jimin] Right?

114
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,407
[Eunsil] Yeah!

115
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:26,576
Can't we just eliminate Pani Bottle again?

116
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,287
We can just send him home
and keep things simple.

117
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:30,747
Individual competitions...

118
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,999
I bet there will be
more team-based games ahead.

119
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:34,918
So definitely,

120
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:37,963
I think we'll need to have
alliances going forward.

121
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:41,508
Yeah, if an alliance agrees
to take one person out,

122
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:43,844
-in that case...
-For sure.

123
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:46,388
...they can get that person
eliminated for sure.

124
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:49,766
[mic feedback]

125
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,060
[host] Please gather in the Main Hall.

126
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,772
[mic feedback]

127
00:05:56,982 --> 00:05:59,901
We will now begin the Seeker Vote.

128
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:04,865
Before the vote, we will reveal whether
the Seeker succeeded in their mission.

129
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:10,287
In the previous Main Match,
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves"...

130
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,247
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

131
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:17,002
the Seeker failed.

132
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,506
-Nice!
-[♪ upbeat music playing]

133
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:22,591
Great.

134
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,930
[Eunsil] I was surprised
that the Seeker failed the mission.

135
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:32,017
[Horseking] It just felt great
to hear the Seeker failed.

136
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:36,313
You ended up failing. You failed.

137
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,857
[host] Since the Seeker failed
their mission,

138
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,152
we will now reveal
what the failed mission was.

139
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:45,697
This is a huge penalty.

140
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:50,035
[host] "Get incorrectly tagged
by two players of your choice."

141
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,244
[Horseking] "Get incorrectly tagged"?

142
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:54,289
Ah, so that's what the missions are like.

143
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:56,499
Their goal was to get incorrectly tagged.

144
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:59,169
But they failed that?
How do you even fail that?

145
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:03,798
I don't know since I didn't play the game,
but is that hard to pull off?

146
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:05,634
-It's easy.
-Honestly, I think it's easy.

147
00:07:05,717 --> 00:07:06,801
-It seems so easy.
-It's easy?

148
00:07:06,885 --> 00:07:09,471
Because all you have to do
is get tagged by everyone.

149
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:13,099
If the Seeker gets tagged
by everyone else while they're a Hunter,

150
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:14,517
they've completed the mission.

151
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:17,729
Then, shouldn't we find out
who was trying to get tagged

152
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,939
-on purpose?
-That's the most likely approach.

153
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:23,652
It's a separate mission
that has nothing to do

154
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:26,071
with winning or losing.

155
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,239
Even if they'd pulled it off,
it would've been

156
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:31,159
very difficult for us to know.

157
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:33,495
We probably would've never known.

158
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:36,373
[♪ tense music playing]

159
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:38,792
It says, "if the Seeker
fails their mission," right?

160
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,130
Then, we can rule out
two people as suspects.

161
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:47,425
"The Seeker cannot select themselves."

162
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:51,930
If they fail, the two people they pick
are revealed and ruled out.

163
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:54,974
That's right.
Then, these two will have a lot of clues.

164
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:58,895
The two selected players really need to
remember who they tagged yesterday.

165
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:00,105
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

166
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:04,567
[host] We will now reveal the two players
selected by the Seeker for their mission.

167
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,069
The players chosen by the Seeker are...

168
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:10,782
Hwang Jaegyun

169
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,410
and Shin Jieun.

170
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:16,746
Excluding Hwang Jaegyun and Shin Jieun,

171
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,416
the Seeker candidates
are among the 10 other players.

172
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,793
The Seeker selected two players
other than themselves,

173
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:24,045
so that rules out
Jieun and Jaegyun as suspects.

174
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:26,172
-We're cleared. I'm not the Seeker.
-It's 0%.

175
00:08:26,256 --> 00:08:28,758
[Ddolddol] And I can't be the Seeker
since I already went to prison.

176
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,301
[Dail] The Seeker made the right choice.

177
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:32,512
Jaegyun was obviously
not the Seeker from the start.

178
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,013
[Dail chuckles]

179
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:36,641
[♪ mysterious music playing]

180
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,687
[Eunsil] So here's the thing.

181
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:44,649
"Get incorrectly tagged
by two players of your choice."

182
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:47,027
Right, the Seeker failed that mission.

183
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:48,820
But I never tagged anyone incorrectly.

184
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,280
[Dail] Isn't that possible?

185
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:51,906
-Then, isn't it a prison member?
-What?

186
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,366
-Isn't it a prison member?
-[Jaegyun] It is.

187
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:54,534
-Right?
-[Jaegyun] It could be

188
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:57,120
-among the players from prison.
-[Eunsil] They couldn't play at all.

189
00:08:57,203 --> 00:09:00,999
Even if you're unable to participate
in the Main Match,

190
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:02,792
-it counts as a failure.
-It's a failure.

191
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:05,128
Since they failed,
everyone except Ddolddol,

192
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:07,130
-like Dail and Pani Bottle...
-[Eunsil] They're included.

193
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,423
-...are included again.
-[Eunsil] Right.

194
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:10,508
-[indistinct chatter]
-Yes, again.

195
00:09:11,176 --> 00:09:12,427
Then, Yang Dail...

196
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:13,970
[Ddolddol] One thing is clear.

197
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,389
The prison members
couldn't participate anyway.

198
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:19,434
And my alibi
from the first Seeker Vote was proven.

199
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,227
-Us three should be ruled out.
-The thing is...

200
00:09:21,311 --> 00:09:23,688
According to the Seeker rules,

201
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:28,443
not participating in the Main Match
also counts as a mission failure.

202
00:09:29,194 --> 00:09:30,195
Ah...

203
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:33,698
[Jaegyun] It's highlighted as a key detail
at the very bottom.

204
00:09:33,782 --> 00:09:37,410
If the mission was a success,
all prison members would've been cleared,

205
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,080
because they couldn't participate.

206
00:09:40,163 --> 00:09:41,289
But at the end of the day,

207
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:44,375
no matter how much we talk about this,

208
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:46,211
-we're the only ones who know.
-[Jaegyun] Right.

209
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:48,588
But from our perspective,

210
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:51,049
we can't completely rule out
the prison members,

211
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:54,219
even if it's only 1% or 2% possible.

212
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:56,179
-The possibility isn't zero.
-Exactly.

213
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,889
-But it's extremely unlikely.
-[Jaegyun] Right.

214
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,516
Do we really need to consider that?

215
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:00,892
[Jaegyun] The chances are very slim.

216
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,227
[Ddolddol] The Seeker? Seriously?

217
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:04,062
I was so annoyed.

218
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:06,314
I can't stand how annoying the Seeker is.

219
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:10,944
I bet you heard this and narrowed it down.

220
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,779
Does everyone have one in mind?

221
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:14,781
I'm a little confused.

222
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:16,866
But it definitely narrowed down, right?

223
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:22,455
She lost in the game, but she was
the one who really came at me.

224
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,125
ZZONE? Right, I was pretty surprised too.

225
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:27,877
[Horseking] It'd make sense
if she went after us as a Hunter,

226
00:10:27,961 --> 00:10:29,629
but she did it when she was a Dog.

227
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,005
It wasn't a wrong tag.

228
00:10:31,089 --> 00:10:32,173
[Jaegyun] That'd be a weird strategy.

229
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,342
When I saw the Seeker's mission,

230
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:37,053
[Sanghyun] I thought we could
narrow things down a little.

231
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:40,098
Considering the mission
was to get incorrectly tagged,

232
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:44,644
it should be someone
who was around Jaegyun and Jieun a lot.

233
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:49,232
If we rule people out,
it has to be someone

234
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:52,527
who challenged Jaegyun
or got tagged by him.

235
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:56,030
In the first round,
those who did that were

236
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:58,950
these two, ZZONE and Joonsu.

237
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:02,412
Someone who was aggressive
when they were a Hunter in Round 1

238
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:05,623
might have held back in Round 2
due to too many negative points.

239
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,251
[ZZONE] Jimin got tagged by eight people.

240
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:09,961
In Round 1?

241
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:12,338
[ZZONE] She got tagged by eight people
when she was a Hunter.

242
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,716
Everyone except Jaegyun tagged her.

243
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,467
[Jimin screams]

244
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,012
No, wait a minute.

245
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,014
JIMIN WAS TAGGED MORE THAN ANYONE ELSE

246
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,765
-No, hold on! [pants]
-[ZZONE] Let's go.

247
00:11:22,849 --> 00:11:26,477
Even if she was a Hunter,
she walked around so freely.

248
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:30,356
[Jimin] Well, look at this. Of all people,
ZZONE is coming after me.

249
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:33,318
No, I didn't tag Jimin.

250
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,862
-I never got tagged by Horseking.
-[Jaegyun] Not me.

251
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:39,574
So when Jimin was a Hunter,
her strategy wasn't to tag others.

252
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:41,701
It was to get tagged to lower our scores.

253
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,536
-I hid the whole time aside from that.
-[Jaegyun] Yeah.

254
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:48,625
Did either Jaegyun
or Jieun incorrectly tag you?

255
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:50,752
-[ZZONE] Jieun did.
-I didn't tag Jimin.

256
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:52,629
-[ZZONE] Jieun did.
-I didn't tag her.

257
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:57,342
But there is this possibility

258
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,427
if I may cautiously suggest this.

259
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:02,138
There's a chance the Seeker
picked Jaegyun and Jieun

260
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,432
to fail the mission intentionally.

261
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:07,769
-You have a point.
-Because if I were the Seeker,

262
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:09,771
-I wouldn't want to clear every mission.
-[♪ serious music playing]

263
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:10,897
That would make me

264
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,649
-look especially suspicious.
-[ZZONE] Right.

265
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:17,237
With that in mind, if you win
and clear the Seeker mission too,

266
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,947
that will look too obvious.

267
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,741
So you'd have to give one up.

268
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:26,871
But revealing two people like that
confirms they're not the Seeker.

269
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:30,208
Isn't ruling out two people
a huge risk for the Seeker?

270
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,670
The Seeker may have decided
to give up on the mission from the start.

271
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:36,422
They could've considered that
and picked the two people

272
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:38,258
who'd be hurt the least by revealing...

273
00:12:38,341 --> 00:12:40,510
[Ddolddol] They could've revealed people
they were okay with revealing.

274
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:42,804
Then, we can't rule anyone out.

275
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:44,347
They could be someone who didn't try

276
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:48,101
or someone who genuinely tried
and just failed.

277
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:49,435
That could apply to any of us.

278
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:51,562
[Ddolddol] Right, so it's hard to tell.

279
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:53,231
The Seeker is too good at this game.

280
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:57,443
That's when I realized,
"This Seeker is on another level."

281
00:12:57,527 --> 00:13:01,781
As for the prison members,
Pani Bottle and Yang Dail,

282
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:05,827
there's no reason
to rule them out as suspects.

283
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:10,581
If anything, this gives us a reason
to suspect them even more.

284
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:15,837
Let's go upstairs and talk.

285
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,882
There's no point in listening to them.
Just for a minute.

286
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:22,593
THE PRISON ALLIANCE STEPS AWAY

287
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:26,514
Even if we hear about yesterday,
we won't really know what happened.

288
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:31,185
Ddolddol and I were constantly
suspicious of Sanghyun.

289
00:13:31,269 --> 00:13:36,232
Every single thing Sanghyun did
seemed really suspicious to me.

290
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:40,945
Just check out
where he's standing right now.

291
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:46,200
He's in the perfect spot to keep an eye
on everyone's movements.

292
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:49,704
If I were the Seeker, I'd stand there
to monitor where everyone was going.

293
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:51,789
Since yesterday, I've noticed

294
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:54,500
he gets really anxious
when people start splitting up.

295
00:13:54,584 --> 00:13:58,796
I ended up in prison last time
because my political play failed.

296
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:02,759
This time, I really need to
handle the politics carefully

297
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:04,302
and get the votes I need.

298
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:06,220
[Pani Bottle] Joonsu.

299
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,680
Come here for a second.

300
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:13,478
[Sanghyun] I was like, "Do they have
something to discuss privately?"

301
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,159
[Dail] Jaegyun.

302
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,911
[ZZONE] So
they're definitely not the Seeker.

303
00:14:32,497 --> 00:14:35,541
I should go talk to the people upstairs.

304
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:38,336
THE GROUP WHO GATHERED LAST NIGHT

305
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:43,341
[Sanghyun] I couldn't forget the look
in Ddolddol's eyes.

306
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:46,302
It seemed like people were divided.

307
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,554
Are we sticking with the plan
or thinking a bit more?

308
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:50,014
[Ddolddol] I don't think
we need to think more.

309
00:14:50,098 --> 00:14:51,724
Without thinking, the prison team

310
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:52,809
-will stick with it.
-[Dail] Jaegyun.

311
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,310
I guarantee you.

312
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:55,937
-I felt it too just now.
-Just now?

313
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:58,815
I went from 99% to 99.9%.

314
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,399
[Junseo] They might have failed.

315
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:02,235
The prison team too...

316
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:03,611
But there are more of them.

317
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:04,737
[Sanghyun] But the prison team...

318
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:08,407
-They didn't play the game.
-[Junseo] Two were revealed here.

319
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:10,743
SANGHYUN COMES
TO WHERE THE PRISON MEMBERS ARE

320
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:11,994
[Sanghyun] Who could it be from prison?

321
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:13,496
Their instincts are terrible.

322
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,664
THE PRISON ALLIANCE LEAVES RIGHT AWAY

323
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:15,915
[sighs]

324
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:22,171
-[Junseo] It's the obvious choice.
-[Sanghyun] Yeah, honestly.

325
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:23,548
Let's check first.

326
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:24,632
I have no doubt.

327
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,552
[Ddolddol] Trust the trend.

328
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:31,097
[Dail] I want you to trust us
on this, ZZONE.

329
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,181
[ZZONE] For the vote?

330
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:33,724
[Dail] Let's at least check.

331
00:15:33,808 --> 00:15:36,519
[ZZONE] Because it would clear two people
as not being the Seeker?

332
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,647
[Sanghyun] Am I under suspicion right now?

333
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,232
-[ZZONE] What?
-Am I under suspicion?

334
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:42,316
Hell yeah, you are.

335
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,318
-Me?
-[ZZONE] Yeah.

336
00:15:44,402 --> 00:15:46,154
-Why?
-Who is?

337
00:15:46,237 --> 00:15:47,238
[ZZONE] The prison team.

338
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,531
The prison team?

339
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:49,657
[Sanghyun] Why?

340
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:55,621
I'm not sure why exactly,
but let's find out together.

341
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,500
-[sighs]
-[ZZONE chuckles]

342
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:04,964
[Sanghyun] I realized that opinions
created by gaslighting

343
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:08,217
can turn into something powerful
and scary when they pile up.

344
00:16:08,301 --> 00:16:10,970
[Junseo] Pani Bottle,
who seems the most suspicious to you?

345
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:12,889
[Pani Bottle] I voted based on
what I believed was right.

346
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:14,348
-You voted?
-Yes, I did.

347
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:16,475
[Sanghyun] So the prison team
is just voting

348
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:19,228
regardless of what we discussed
in the Main Match?

349
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:21,189
What we've heard
hasn't really convinced us.

350
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:22,273
We're not sure.

351
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:23,733
[Sanghyun] You wouldn't know
what was a fact?

352
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:26,068
Exactly. Even after hearing it,
we don't get it.

353
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:28,654
I don't know the rulebook.
I haven't read it.

354
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,449
[Sanghyun] In the Main Match,
their mission failed.

355
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:32,700
SANGHYUN MAKES HIS CASE

356
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:35,203
So there are people
we can narrow down from this.

357
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:38,831
[Ddolddol] I didn't really listen to him.
I'm sure he's nervous.

358
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:40,750
[Sanghyun] Did you have to vote
so quickly?

359
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,961
I believe the Seeker
will be caught eventually.

360
00:16:44,879 --> 00:16:49,008
-They'll be caught at some point.
-They have a completely different mindset.

361
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,177
They're extremely stubborn.

362
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:54,931
They're so stubborn
that it's impossible to convince them.

363
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:56,098
If they're cleared, then good.

364
00:16:56,182 --> 00:16:57,934
-If not, it gets complicated.
-Yeah.

365
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,436
[Pani Bottle] We can't force anyone.

366
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:03,356
All we can do is try to persuade others
or make our case.

367
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:06,150
We can't blame others
for not doing what we wanted.

368
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:09,111
I didn't really have anything else to say.

369
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,447
-Can I ask you something?
-[Horseking] What?

370
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:12,740
[Sanghyun] Do you still suspect me?

371
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:16,244
To be honest,
it's not even about suspicion.

372
00:17:16,327 --> 00:17:18,246
-[Sanghyun] Okay.
-It's based on the circumstances.

373
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,164
[Sanghyun] Am I included in that?

374
00:17:20,248 --> 00:17:21,249
Of course.

375
00:17:21,332 --> 00:17:22,792
-From the start...
-[Sanghyun] But why?

376
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:26,295
I just don't get it.
Their mission failed in the Main Match.

377
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:28,965
I never even showed you my back.

378
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,716
That's true. So, we were saying...

379
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,343
[Sanghyun] And I avoided Jieun
the whole time.

380
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:33,469
SANGHYUN GETS WORKED UP

381
00:17:33,553 --> 00:17:36,264
If I were the Seeker, I'd just get tagged.
Why bother tagging her too?

382
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:37,807
[Horseking] She did suddenly
come after you.

383
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,059
Exactly. That's why I think...

384
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:41,143
You come with me.

385
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:43,479
[Sanghyun] I'm upset.

386
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:45,106
[Eunsil] Why?

387
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,816
[Sanghyun] Because of the prison team.

388
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,109
[Eunsil] They all pinned it on you.

389
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,444
[Sanghyun] I mean,
I don't care if they suspect me.

390
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:52,822
But we can figure things out
based on the clues.

391
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:55,616
[Eunsil] The prison team seems
dead set on voting you out.

392
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,742
[Sanghyun] I know.

393
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:58,661
[smacks lips, sighs]

394
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:03,583
[Sanghyun] Everyone's been suspecting me
as the Seeker

395
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,459
ever since day one,

396
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:07,336
so I was mentally exhausted.

397
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:11,507
I no longer had the chance
to convince people anymore.

398
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,513
THE VOTES ARE LEANING TOWARD SANGHYUN

399
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,473
[sighs wearily]

400
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:26,897
PLAYERS CAST THEIR VOTES RIGHT AWAY

401
00:18:26,981 --> 00:18:28,065
Hello.

402
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:30,318
Please vote for who you think
is the Seeker.

403
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:33,738
SEEKER VOTE
YOUN SANGHYUN

404
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,406
[Sanghyun] Did Jimin vote?

405
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:37,366
-[Jimin] Sanghyun.
-[Sanghyun] Yeah? Come here.

406
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:39,869
To be honest, I'm a little mad.

407
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,120
[Jimin] Why?

408
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,580
[Sanghyun] We could've figured things out.

409
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:44,332
-We could've narrowed it down.
-[Jimin] Right.

410
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,666
[Sanghyun] I was so frustrated.

411
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:48,586
I thought you played
an amazing game yesterday.

412
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:53,382
I know you're frustrated and upset,
but it's because you played so well.

413
00:18:54,175 --> 00:18:57,470
And if you're actually the Seeker,
then you played it really well.

414
00:18:58,721 --> 00:19:00,473
[Sanghyun] I'm really losing my cool.

415
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,441
[sighs] Seriously.

416
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,029
[host] Voting has ended.

417
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,366
Please gather in the Main Hall.

418
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:21,077
[Pani Bottle sighs heavily]

419
00:19:25,373 --> 00:19:28,125
[Dail] I was 100% sure it was Sanghyun,

420
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:30,294
so I just watched his reaction.

421
00:19:30,378 --> 00:19:33,422
I was thinking to myself,
"It's you, isn't it?" [laughs]

422
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,300
[Ddolddol] I'm 99% sure
it's Youn Sanghyun.

423
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:41,347
[host] Here is the result.
The player who received the most votes...

424
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,725
is Youn Sanghyun.

425
00:19:46,936 --> 00:19:48,312
[sighs]

426
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:52,316
[Ddolddol] This time,
I succeeded in playing politics.

427
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:55,986
[host] Your attempt to catch the Seeker...

428
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,408
has failed.

429
00:20:07,248 --> 00:20:09,083
[Sanghyun] I kept saying it wasn't me.

430
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,252
[host] Due to failure
to capture the Seeker,

431
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:15,548
we will reveal the elimination candidate
chosen by the Seeker.

432
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:20,010
The elimination candidate
chosen by the Seeker...

433
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,475
is Youn Sanghyun.

434
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:27,727
[players] What?

435
00:20:27,810 --> 00:20:28,811
[Joonsu] Again?

436
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:30,396
What?

437
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,857
-What?
-[Joonsu] Again?

438
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:34,984
[Jaegyun exclaims]

439
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,406
[Eunsil] The Seeker had already voted,

440
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,533
knowing Sanghyun
would be up for the Seeker Vote.

441
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:43,951
Seriously, who is it?

442
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:48,914
The Seeker is really smart.

443
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:52,418
[Ddolddol] I truly felt so bad.

444
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:54,712
I thought maybe I should beg
for forgiveness.

445
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:56,589
I'm so sorry.

446
00:20:57,715 --> 00:21:01,010
[host] Youn Sanghyun,
please leave the area immediately.

447
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:04,013
Sanghyun. [laughs]

448
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:06,432
I'll come visit you.

449
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:09,310
[♪ suspenseful string music playing]

450
00:21:10,186 --> 00:21:11,729
[Sanghyun] Ah...

451
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:15,649
Honestly, I'm really mad
at the other players.

452
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:18,319
[fake whimpering]

453
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:20,404
Ah, unbelievable.

454
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:22,740
[sighs]

455
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:25,910
They didn't vote
based on their own judgment

456
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,120
and followed the crowd instead.

457
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:29,497
I just don't get it.

458
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:34,043
I just want to beat them all.

459
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:37,671
[Pani Bottle] By the way... [sighs]

460
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:40,382
-I'm a little shocked.
-[Dail] It is shocking.

461
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:43,302
[Jaegyun sighs] I'm so confused.

462
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:45,137
So the Seeker is among us right now.

463
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:46,347
No way, no way.

464
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:48,891
[Eunsil] I'm so annoyed.

465
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:52,019
[Horseking sighs] What's going on?

466
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:59,777
We can't help but think now
the Seeker could be among the prison team.

467
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,946
That's on the table now.

468
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:04,198
I think we need
to start reconsidering everyone

469
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,575
except the ones we know for sure.

470
00:22:06,659 --> 00:22:09,703
The Seeker's playing us right now.

471
00:22:10,538 --> 00:22:12,873
How does this keep happening
every single time?

472
00:22:12,957 --> 00:22:15,209
[♪ music surges]

473
00:22:15,292 --> 00:22:18,462
[Horseking] The Seeker is always
way ahead of us.

474
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:21,799
I feel like we're being controlled
by the Seeker.

475
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:23,300
It really hurt my pride.

476
00:22:23,384 --> 00:22:25,803
At that point,
I didn't care about winning.

477
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:28,514
I just wanted to catch the Seeker.
I was so annoyed.

478
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:29,932
[groans]

479
00:22:31,559 --> 00:22:33,477
The Seeker is really smart.

480
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:35,020
It's so annoying.

481
00:22:35,104 --> 00:22:39,108
If I catch them, I want to punch them.
That's how I felt.

482
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:41,402
[Pani Bottle] Right now,
the totally innocent ones

483
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,404
are Ddolddol, Jaegyun, and Sanghyun.

484
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,447
It's not me either. I'm totally innocent.

485
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:47,533
No, it still could be you two.

486
00:22:47,616 --> 00:22:49,702
-[Jimin] It's possible.
-Even if it's only 1%,

487
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:50,953
it's still a possibility.

488
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:53,789
[Pani Bottle] It's not impossible,
but we're honestly at 1%.

489
00:22:53,873 --> 00:22:57,001
If I turn out to be the Seeker,
I'll literally cut off my arms and legs.

490
00:22:58,335 --> 00:22:59,545
Maybe it's Dail.

491
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:01,964
-Come on, why are you doing this?
-[Eunsil] It's you, isn't it?

492
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:04,466
-Dail, it's you, isn't it?
-[Dail] I wish it were me.

493
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,760
You're making yourself more suspicious.
Just be quiet.

494
00:23:06,844 --> 00:23:08,095
Fine, you can suspect me.

495
00:23:08,178 --> 00:23:10,264
But the more you do,
the more dumb you look.

496
00:23:10,347 --> 00:23:12,725
[♪ music intensifies]

497
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:17,688
[groans softly]
They're hopeless. For crying out loud.

498
00:23:19,273 --> 00:23:20,816
Gosh, they're so hopeless. [chuckles]

499
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:24,778
-[Pani Bottle] I'm the same.
-I'll bet my life on it.

500
00:23:27,615 --> 00:23:31,201
If you say that, we'll all do the same.
We'll bet our lives too.

501
00:23:31,285 --> 00:23:32,912
I'll really bet my life on it. Will you?

502
00:23:32,995 --> 00:23:33,996
I will.

503
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:39,168
[host] According to the rules
of Deadly Tag,

504
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:40,669
you have become the Seeker.

505
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,385
Now, manipulate the game,

506
00:23:48,469 --> 00:23:50,179
SURVIVE WITHOUT REVEALING YOUR IDENTITY

507
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:53,432
and create chaos
to prevent the players from winning.

508
00:23:56,769 --> 00:24:00,606
SEEKER PARK JIMIN

509
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:08,072
Seriously, am I meant to be a spy?

510
00:24:13,702 --> 00:24:14,703
BEFORE THE FIRST MAIN MATCH

511
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:17,665
[dealer] Please choose a locker number
from 1 to 12 to store your funds.

512
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:19,416
PLAYERS CHOSE KEYS
AFTER DEPOSITING FUNDS

513
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:20,751
I'll go with No. 4.

514
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:24,463
THE IDENTITY OF KEY NO. 4

515
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:30,844
YOU HAVE BECOME THE SEEKER

516
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:33,889
[Jimin] It said,
"You're the Seeker," so I thought,

517
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:36,350
"Am I the only one who got this message?"

518
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:37,726
"I'm the only one?"

519
00:24:37,810 --> 00:24:39,478
I was really flustered.

520
00:24:40,229 --> 00:24:44,817
But these kinds of games with politics
are pretty much my forte.

521
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,235
And with a battle of wits.

522
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:51,115
When I saw the mission,
I knew I had to help the Cops win.

523
00:24:51,198 --> 00:24:52,950
MAIN MATCH, "COPS AND ROBBERS"
SEEKER MISSION

524
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,410
I thought it over really quickly.

525
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:55,494
MAKE THREE COPS WIN

526
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:59,581
My first thought was,
"Who got the ropes off first?"

527
00:24:59,665 --> 00:25:00,666
1ST: YOUN SANGHYUN

528
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:02,334
2ND: JANG EUNSIL

529
00:25:02,418 --> 00:25:05,713
Also, Yuk Junseo is a former UDT member,

530
00:25:05,796 --> 00:25:09,008
and this game requires physical strength.

531
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:15,597
THREE COPS SELECTED

532
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:18,142
First off, I wanted to make sure
the cops won.

533
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:20,352
ROUND 1

534
00:25:20,436 --> 00:25:24,023
As soon as Round 1 started,
I got caught so quickly.

535
00:25:24,106 --> 00:25:27,109
SEEKER'S HELP 1
MAKE YOURSELF EASY FOR THE COPS TO FIND

536
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,235
Geez, you scared me.

537
00:25:29,695 --> 00:25:32,197
-[Eunsil clears throat]
-[Jimin] She's good.

538
00:25:33,866 --> 00:25:35,117
I picked good cops.

539
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,829
You're a Drug Criminal.

540
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:42,291
No, I'm not.

541
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:43,542
[Eunsil] You're not, even with this?

542
00:25:43,625 --> 00:25:45,210
SEEKER'S HELP 2
WEAK LIES IN INTERROGATION

543
00:25:45,294 --> 00:25:46,587
[Jimin] No, I'm an Assault Criminal.

544
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:51,091
With lies this obvious,
she must've caught on.

545
00:25:51,175 --> 00:25:53,302
-[Pani Bottle] That's impressive.
-[Dail] You're good.

546
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:55,304
[ZZONE] The Cops did such a great job.

547
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:57,097
[Jimin] I was proud of them.

548
00:25:57,639 --> 00:26:01,477
How did the cops get such a good lineup?
It's because I picked them.

549
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:07,149
Everyone thinks the cops made it happen
on their own, but I set everything up.

550
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:10,027
I built this whole thing
and made them what they are.

551
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:12,529
[Sanghyun] Where's Horseking?

552
00:26:12,613 --> 00:26:14,239
PLAYERS RETURN AFTER THE MAIN MATCH

553
00:26:14,323 --> 00:26:17,826
SEEKER PARK JIMIN IS BUSY
BEHIND THE SCENES

554
00:26:18,911 --> 00:26:22,623
THE MAP PROVIDED TO THE SEEKER

555
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:27,336
[Jimin] The map showed lockers,
a table, and a secret room.

556
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:28,420
LOCKERS

557
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:35,344
Then, I noticed a red light
behind the lockers.

558
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:38,472
So I shoved the lockers
really hard to the side.

559
00:26:38,555 --> 00:26:40,849
[♪ thrilling synth music playing]

560
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:43,769
THE SECRET SEEKER ROOM
BEHIND THE VOTING ROOM

561
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:50,734
I had no idea there was a room behind it.

562
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:53,320
Wow, it was really thrilling.

563
00:26:53,403 --> 00:26:56,865
It felt like I had
an incredible privilege.

564
00:26:57,866 --> 00:27:01,120
[host] Tonight, the first Seeker Vote
will take place.

565
00:27:01,995 --> 00:27:05,040
Select a player
who will face the Elimination Vote.

566
00:27:05,541 --> 00:27:10,379
[Jimin] I thought about
how Kim Ddolddol won the game

567
00:27:10,462 --> 00:27:13,090
by cleverly betraying Joonsu.

568
00:27:13,173 --> 00:27:15,592
-That's why it's easy to frame him.
-Sorry.

569
00:27:15,676 --> 00:27:17,010
It's because we have evidence.

570
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:19,179
So, I picked Kim Ddolddol.

571
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:20,305
TARGET: KIM DDOLDDOL

572
00:27:20,931 --> 00:27:22,724
TALKING BEFORE THE SEEKER VOTE

573
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:24,434
[Jieun] The Seeker
was manipulating the game.

574
00:27:24,518 --> 00:27:27,104
-Just to give my honest opinion,
-[♪ rock music playing]

575
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:29,523
I have a feeling it's Sanghyun.

576
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:32,818
[Jimin] He started suspecting Sanghyun,

577
00:27:32,901 --> 00:27:35,112
so I thought, "Thank you."

578
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:37,114
If he'll put himself out there,
I'm all for it.

579
00:27:37,197 --> 00:27:40,033
-Kim Ddolddol was getting too involved.
-[ZZONE] To be honest,

580
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:42,244
-I was suspicious of him too.
-I know.

581
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:43,328
But I think

582
00:27:43,412 --> 00:27:44,663
"CASTING SUSPICION ON DDOLDDOL"

583
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:46,498
after hearing what Ddolddol said...

584
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:48,125
[Eunsil] I'm suspicious of Ddolddol too.

585
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:49,710
I suspected Ddolddol from the start.

586
00:27:49,793 --> 00:27:53,338
[Jimin] Wow, this is great luck.
It'll be perfect for me to pile on.

587
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:57,509
If we all agree on one person to vote for,

588
00:27:57,593 --> 00:27:59,136
that person will definitely be out.

589
00:27:59,219 --> 00:28:00,929
Yeah, they'll definitely be out.

590
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:03,181
Then, how about we all vote
for the same person?

591
00:28:03,724 --> 00:28:05,559
I agree with voting for Ddolddol.

592
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:09,688
[Jimin] I casually suggested it,
and everyone agreed.

593
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:12,816
I think that took barely a minute.

594
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:16,194
[dealer] As you successfully cleared
the Seeker mission yesterday,

595
00:28:16,278 --> 00:28:18,989
you receive one extra voting ticket.

596
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:23,076
That's right. The Seeker gets two.

597
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:27,414
KIM DDOLDDOL CONFIRMED
AS ELIMINATION CANDIDATE

598
00:28:27,497 --> 00:28:28,832
[Jimin] I expected it.

599
00:28:28,916 --> 00:28:33,128
I picked the person
people would most likely suspect.

600
00:28:34,171 --> 00:28:37,049
Looking back,
I actually picked really well.

601
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:47,809
[dealer] Please name two players
who will incorrectly tag you.

602
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:51,605
Shin Jieun and Hwang Jaegyun.

603
00:28:52,522 --> 00:28:56,610
[host] In the previous Main Match,
the Seeker failed.

604
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:58,236
-[Joonsu] Nice!
-[players cheering]

605
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,696
[♪ ominous music playing]

606
00:29:00,489 --> 00:29:01,490
Great.

607
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:05,953
[Jimin] My strategy
was basically a fake-out.

608
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,997
[Horseking] For today's Seeker Vote,
I'll say this confidently.

609
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:11,166
It has to be out of ZZONE,
Jieun, and Jimin.

610
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:14,127
[Jimin] Horseking seemed to have locked in
who the Seeker could be

611
00:29:14,211 --> 00:29:16,213
and was starting to suspect us.

612
00:29:16,296 --> 00:29:19,091
That makes no sense. No, sorry, sorry.

613
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:20,759
Not including prison members, right?

614
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:23,387
It could be someone who is in prison.

615
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:26,723
Then, the Seeker mission
would be counted as a failure.

616
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:30,102
[Jimin] Then, the Seeker mission needs
to fail for more suspects to emerge.

617
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:32,646
Once the prison team gets ruled out,

618
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:35,565
I thought I'd be at a disadvantage.

619
00:29:35,649 --> 00:29:38,235
That's why I failed
the Seeker mission on purpose.

620
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:40,237
Because it worked in my favor.

621
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:42,489
[♪ music intensifies]

622
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:47,536
And those up for elimination
turned out exactly the way I wanted.

623
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:51,331
I felt bad, but I had to pull
Sanghyun's card quickly.

624
00:29:51,415 --> 00:29:52,833
So, I chose Sanghyun.

625
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:55,919
YOUN SANGHYUN CONFIRMED
AS ELIMINATION CANDIDATE AS PLANNED

626
00:29:57,587 --> 00:29:58,714
[players] What?

627
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:01,049
-[Joonsu] Again? That's crazy.
-[Dail] The Seeker is so smart.

628
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:02,342
PRETENDING TO BE SURPRISED

629
00:30:02,426 --> 00:30:04,678
[Jimin] I guess
my strategy really paid off.

630
00:30:05,387 --> 00:30:07,931
Could anyone be a better Seeker than me?

631
00:30:08,682 --> 00:30:10,976
I feel like I can keep pushing ahead.

632
00:30:11,059 --> 00:30:14,938
Because I can create
another sacrifice when I need to.

633
00:30:15,022 --> 00:30:18,775
If I keep going like this,
I should be fine going forward.

634
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:21,486
[Pani Bottle sighs loudly]

635
00:30:23,113 --> 00:30:25,282
-[♪ contemplative music playing]
-The Seeker is pretty good.

636
00:30:25,365 --> 00:30:28,827
The fact that we're getting annoyed
proves that the Seeker's doing a good job.

637
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:30,370
I know. I'm annoyed too.

638
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:31,788
[groans]

639
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:33,999
[sighs in exasperation]

640
00:30:34,082 --> 00:30:35,542
This is getting on my nerves.

641
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:41,965
[mic feedback]

642
00:30:42,049 --> 00:30:46,845
[host] Tomorrow's Main Match
will be a five-on-five team battle.

643
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:49,973
[players gasp]

644
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:54,394
The winning team will receive
20 million won in personal funds

645
00:30:55,062 --> 00:30:57,773
and an Elimination Immunity Pass
for each member.

646
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,483
-[ZZONE] All five survive?
-Five players?

647
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:01,109
[Pani Bottle] The whole teams advances.

648
00:31:02,736 --> 00:31:04,488
[host] And the losing team

649
00:31:06,615 --> 00:31:08,700
-will all be up for elimination
-[ZZONE gasps loudly]

650
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:12,079
-and go straight to the Death Match.
-Six people right away.

651
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:14,372
We're having the Death Match
immediately tomorrow.

652
00:31:14,456 --> 00:31:17,626
[host] The game will take place
around each team's base.

653
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:22,380
Each team will have one leader
representing them.

654
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:25,300
-Who will be the leader?
-[Horseking] Who's the leader?

655
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:30,138
[host] We will announce the team leaders
for tomorrow's Main Match.

656
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:34,184
Kim Ddolddol.

657
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:40,690
-I can't handle this pressure! Please!
-[all laughing]

658
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:42,984
It was too much pressure for me.

659
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:44,611
Why did I get picked?

660
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:46,113
Isn't it going to be Pani Bottle?

661
00:31:46,238 --> 00:31:48,115
WHO'S THE OTHER LEADER?

662
00:31:49,783 --> 00:31:51,618
And ZZONE.

663
00:31:52,244 --> 00:31:55,455
-Me?
-[players exclaiming]

664
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:57,833
What's the criteria for this?

665
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:02,337
[host] The team leaders
were personally chosen by the Seeker.

666
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:03,880
[♪ intriguing music playing]

667
00:32:03,964 --> 00:32:05,590
I knew it.

668
00:32:05,674 --> 00:32:07,259
Wow.

669
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:11,680
[host] The two team leaders will draw lots
to decide the order,

670
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:16,309
and then take turns selecting
one team member at a time.

671
00:32:16,393 --> 00:32:17,853
[Jaegyun] Oh...

672
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:21,481
[host] Team selections
will start in an hour.

673
00:32:23,733 --> 00:32:26,695
[beeping]

674
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,281
Man, this is strange.

675
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:33,493
Why make those two the leaders?

676
00:32:33,577 --> 00:32:34,870
That I don't know.

677
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:38,957
[Pani Bottle]
The choice of leaders really puzzled me.

678
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:43,253
Because normally, they'd split up
the two strongest players.

679
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:48,216
ZZONE wasn't considered a strong player,
so the fact that she became a leader

680
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:52,053
only made sense if she was the Seeker.

681
00:32:52,137 --> 00:32:54,139
The Seeker would want
to create a strong team.

682
00:32:54,890 --> 00:32:59,603
We know he's not the Seeker.
The Seeker could pick themselves.

683
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,647
ZZONE SUSPECTED AS THE SEEKER

684
00:33:02,731 --> 00:33:06,276
[ZZONE] At first, I was really surprised
when I suddenly became a leader.

685
00:33:06,359 --> 00:33:11,531
I felt like the Seeker suspects
were starting to narrow down.

686
00:33:11,615 --> 00:33:16,703
And it seemed like there was an intention
to include me as a suspect.

687
00:33:16,786 --> 00:33:19,247
[Ddolddol] Kim Ddolddol, ZZONE.

688
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:25,170
What? Usually, they'd pick people
with similar traits.

689
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:30,342
Those two are kind of total opposites.

690
00:33:30,425 --> 00:33:33,803
I didn't think Kim Ddolddol and ZZONE
made sense as a leader pairing.

691
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:38,516
[exasperated sigh]
This is giving me a headache.

692
00:33:40,310 --> 00:33:42,312
This was all part of my bigger plan.

693
00:33:44,314 --> 00:33:47,484
ONE HOUR AGO

694
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,569
[Joonsu] I'm curious
about the game tomorrow.

695
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:51,404
Where is everybody?

696
00:33:52,781 --> 00:33:54,199
Should I bring Eunsil over?

697
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:57,410
-[♪ suspicious music playing]
-[Joonsu singing ballad music]

698
00:33:57,911 --> 00:33:58,912
Eunsil...

699
00:33:58,995 --> 00:34:01,122
PARK JIMIN LEAVES THE DINING ROOM

700
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:02,415
Where's Eunsil?

701
00:34:03,083 --> 00:34:05,543
LOOKING AROUND

702
00:34:05,627 --> 00:34:07,003
This game is really hard.

703
00:34:07,087 --> 00:34:08,338
THE TWO HAVEN'T NOTICED ANYTHING

704
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:12,133
SHE SNEAKS OUT
PRETENDING TO LOOK FOR EUNSIL

705
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:15,971
DEADLY TAG
SEEKER RULES

706
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:18,014
JIMIN SECRETLY ENTERED THE SEEKER ROOM

707
00:34:21,101 --> 00:34:23,478
[exhales] This is driving me crazy.

708
00:34:24,562 --> 00:34:26,147
THIRD MAIN MATCH
SEEKER MISSION

709
00:34:26,231 --> 00:34:28,483
SELECT TWO TEAM LEADERS
WHO WILL FORM THE TEAMS

710
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:29,943
[whispers] Leader...

711
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:36,074
PICKED KIM DDOLDDOL IMMEDIATELY
AS THE FIRST LEADER

712
00:34:36,157 --> 00:34:40,161
First of all, the prison group,
Kim Ddolddol, Yang Dail, and Pani Bottle,

713
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:42,080
seemed to have a really strong bond.

714
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:44,249
They'd been sticking together all day,

715
00:34:44,874 --> 00:34:48,586
so I figured those three
were definitely going to team up.

716
00:34:48,670 --> 00:34:52,090
But I didn't want to join their team.

717
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:55,010
Honestly, I wanted to be the one
picking the team members.

718
00:34:55,093 --> 00:34:58,972
But people were already getting
a little suspicious of me.

719
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:03,518
So I thought about who would choose me...

720
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:09,065
PICKED ZZONE AS THE SECOND LEADER

721
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:11,610
I felt like I could trust ZZONE the most

722
00:35:11,693 --> 00:35:14,529
since we had been sharing a room
from the very beginning.

723
00:35:14,613 --> 00:35:18,658
And us girls talk about
a lot of things in our room.

724
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:21,077
[ZZONE] The prison alliance
seems really strong.

725
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:22,537
[Jimin] Their bond is no joke.

726
00:35:22,621 --> 00:35:25,248
I think we need to have each other's backs

727
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:27,542
if we're going to get through the game.

728
00:35:27,626 --> 00:35:28,627
I agree.

729
00:35:28,710 --> 00:35:30,462
[Eunsil] We need
to eliminate them all quickly,

730
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:32,213
starting with the prison family.

731
00:35:32,297 --> 00:35:37,177
Since ZZONE was on the list
of possible Seekers,

732
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:40,722
I thought picking her could be a way
to make people suspect she was the Seeker.

733
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:42,932
That's why I picked ZZONE.

734
00:35:44,559 --> 00:35:47,937
THINGS SEEM TO GO
ACCORDING TO JIMIN'S PLAN

735
00:35:48,647 --> 00:35:50,482
Is there really anything to discuss?

736
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:52,400
Isn't it up to whoever's picking?

737
00:35:52,484 --> 00:35:53,610
[Jaegyun] What's there to talk about?

738
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:54,736
GETS UP

739
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:57,113
We're supposed to talk about
who will be on which team.

740
00:35:57,197 --> 00:35:58,323
SLOWLY WALKING

741
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:01,159
-After drawing lots...
-[♪ suspicious music playing]

742
00:36:02,535 --> 00:36:07,290
SIGNALS KIM DDOLDDOL WITH A HAND GESTURE

743
00:36:07,374 --> 00:36:09,084
[indistinct chatter]

744
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:11,252
[Pani Bottle] It might be hard
to get the prison group together.

745
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:13,672
-I wonder if we can.
-[Pani Bottle] Right? That'd be ideal.

746
00:36:14,381 --> 00:36:17,092
YANG DAIL WALKS OUT SHORTLY AFTER

747
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:20,970
[Jimin] They kept passing by
to have their own discussions.

748
00:36:21,805 --> 00:36:23,598
I picked really well.

749
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:26,226
[Pani Bottle] Let's go upstairs.

750
00:36:29,604 --> 00:36:31,981
GLANCES

751
00:36:33,274 --> 00:36:34,359
[Jimin] Look.

752
00:36:34,442 --> 00:36:35,443
JIMIN BEGINS HER OPERATION

753
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,070
-They'll team up for sure, right?
-Sorry?

754
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:38,947
Those three will definitely
team up, right?

755
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,532
Is that possible?

756
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:42,492
Not really, if I pick one of them.

757
00:36:42,575 --> 00:36:45,412
If ZZONE picks one of them,
those three can't stick together.

758
00:36:45,495 --> 00:36:46,621
[ZZONE] It'll divide them up.

759
00:36:46,705 --> 00:36:49,708
They'll assume that I won't pick them.

760
00:36:49,791 --> 00:36:51,334
The entire five-member team

761
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:53,503
-will go to the Death Match.
-[ZZONE] Right.

762
00:36:53,586 --> 00:36:54,629
So maybe the best move

763
00:36:54,713 --> 00:36:57,841
is to take them all out.

764
00:36:57,924 --> 00:37:00,343
Let them stick together
and take them all out?

765
00:37:00,427 --> 00:37:02,846
-Let those three team up like that?
-[Jimin] Yes.

766
00:37:02,929 --> 00:37:04,889
This is when we need Sanghyun.

767
00:37:04,973 --> 00:37:06,307
[♪ amusing music playing]

768
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:07,767
We sent him away.

769
00:37:07,851 --> 00:37:09,102
Poor Sanghyun.

770
00:37:10,270 --> 00:37:12,397
[Horseking] Sanghyun
was a really strong player.

771
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:13,606
[Eunsil] I miss him.

772
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:17,277
[Pani Bottle sighs]

773
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:19,320
[Pani Bottle] They really
complicated things.

774
00:37:19,404 --> 00:37:21,781
[Ddolddol] The three of us
trust each other more than anyone else.

775
00:37:21,865 --> 00:37:23,700
It's best if us three
are on the same team.

776
00:37:23,783 --> 00:37:25,493
[Pani Bottle] We have to stick together.

777
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:27,328
Who else do you think would work well?

778
00:37:27,412 --> 00:37:31,332
Aside from the three of us,
Yuk Junseo, Horseking, or Jaegyun.

779
00:37:31,416 --> 00:37:32,751
Horseking or Jaegyun?

780
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:38,423
Since it's a team match, I want to team up
with Pani Bottle and Yang Dail,

781
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:40,759
my prison mates who I've built
a strong bond with.

782
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:43,428
And we should bring one strong guy.

783
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:49,142
Maybe someone athletic,
like Horseking, Yuk Junseo, or Jaegyun?

784
00:37:49,225 --> 00:37:51,728
The guys will be split up
since ZZONE is going to pick

785
00:37:51,811 --> 00:37:52,937
-the strong ones.
-[Pani Bottle] Right.

786
00:37:53,021 --> 00:37:55,648
Then, who should I pick first?

787
00:37:55,732 --> 00:37:57,484
-In my opinion...
-Jaegyun?

788
00:37:57,567 --> 00:37:59,235
If you win the draw...

789
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:00,904
-Us first?
-No, not us.

790
00:38:00,987 --> 00:38:02,113
Pick Yuk Junseo first.

791
00:38:02,739 --> 00:38:04,199
-As for Yuk Junseo,
-[♪ contemplative music playing]

792
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:07,076
these games require
some physical strength, but...

793
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:09,412
I still believe we need a strong player.

794
00:38:09,913 --> 00:38:12,749
For the next pick,
who first between you two?

795
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,083
Then, you should pick Jaegyun.

796
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:16,544
-What about you two?
-[Dail] You can pick us later.

797
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:20,381
But I think the three of us
have to team up, no matter what.

798
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:22,050
If the three of us join forces,

799
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:25,386
I think we're the strongest team
even without players like Yuk Junseo.

800
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:26,554
And Sanghyun's not around.

801
00:38:26,638 --> 00:38:28,681
If they take one of us,
we're in big trouble.

802
00:38:28,765 --> 00:38:31,267
[Pani Bottle] I really wanted us three
on the same team.

803
00:38:31,351 --> 00:38:35,146
ZZONE definitely knows
that the three of us are tightly united.

804
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:38,650
So I figured she'd try
to split us up somehow.

805
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:40,944
I'm worried it won't be easy
for us to stick together.

806
00:38:41,027 --> 00:38:43,613
[Pani Bottle] I think you should
try to pick us first, if possible.

807
00:38:43,696 --> 00:38:44,697
That's what I think.

808
00:38:44,781 --> 00:38:46,950
That way, we can work as a team.

809
00:38:47,033 --> 00:38:51,663
But what if she picks Yuk Junseo,
Jaegyun, and Horseking all in a row?

810
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:52,831
What then?

811
00:38:58,586 --> 00:39:00,380
THE PRISON ALLIANCE RETURNS
TO THE MAIN HALL

812
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:02,173
What are you going to do, Ddolddol?

813
00:39:02,257 --> 00:39:04,300
-Are the three of you sticking together?
-[Ddolddol] Sorry?

814
00:39:04,384 --> 00:39:06,636
Let me tell you something in advance.

815
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:08,847
-If you pick me for your team...
-Yes?

816
00:39:08,930 --> 00:39:10,640
Then, I'm going to troll.

817
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:12,100
-I'll go to the Death Match.
-[♪ tense music playing]

818
00:39:12,183 --> 00:39:14,185
-I like trolls.
-[Pani Bottle] I'm just telling you.

819
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:16,145
I'm just saying, "Please don't pick me."

820
00:39:16,229 --> 00:39:18,773
If I'm not on Ddolddol's team,
I'll just give up tomorrow

821
00:39:18,857 --> 00:39:20,650
and throw the game.

822
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:23,152
[Horseking] I thought
he was being way too pushy.

823
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:27,198
What's wrong with him?
Why would he say that now?

824
00:39:27,282 --> 00:39:29,242
He really got on my nerves.

825
00:39:29,325 --> 00:39:35,748
Even without us, I don't think
it would create an imbalance.

826
00:39:35,832 --> 00:39:38,543
I agree with you, but it's fun.

827
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:42,297
-It's not fun for me.
-[laughs]

828
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,507
[ZZONE] It was seriously annoying.

829
00:39:44,591 --> 00:39:48,052
So I wanted to break up the alliance
between the three prison players.

830
00:39:48,845 --> 00:39:51,598
[dealer] We will begin team selection.

831
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:55,727
-Ms. ZZONE, you have the first pick.
-[♪ rock music playing]

832
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:58,438
Please name one team member
you would like to select.

833
00:39:59,105 --> 00:40:00,940
The order is really important.

834
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:04,569
If he picks first, then I pick,
then he picks again, and I pick again,

835
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:08,781
my options can change a lot
depending on my position in the order.

836
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:10,658
-I'll pick this one.
-[ZZONE] You first. It's 50-50.

837
00:40:10,742 --> 00:40:11,743
-You want this one?
-[ZZONE] Yes.

838
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,620
-[Ddolddol] Want to switch?
-Shall we?

839
00:40:13,703 --> 00:40:15,330
[Ddolddol] One, two, three.

840
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:19,584
You go first, ZZONE.

841
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:21,169
ZZONE GETS THE RIGHT FOR FIRST PICK

842
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:22,295
[ZZONE] When I drew the 1 card,

843
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:25,506
I thought, "I did it!
I have a chance to win this time."

844
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:26,925
I was so happy.

845
00:40:31,262 --> 00:40:32,263
I'll...

846
00:40:33,056 --> 00:40:35,475
-What's going to happen?
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

847
00:40:36,059 --> 00:40:37,852
Will she sabotage or use her own strategy?

848
00:40:38,728 --> 00:40:40,939
[Jimin] I picked ZZONE.

849
00:40:41,564 --> 00:40:45,151
I really hope she does well.

850
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:49,447
I'll pick Horseking.

851
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:51,074
ZZONE PICKS HORSEKING FIRST

852
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:55,495
For a physical battle, I definitely needed
Horseking on the same team.

853
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:58,957
Ironically enough,
I wanted to be on ZZONE's team.

854
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:02,752
There's a certain synergy between people,
and Ddolddol is somewhat...

855
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:05,672
He's been too talkative since day one.

856
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:10,301
I noticed that he's very vocal
and has his own strong opinions.

857
00:41:10,385 --> 00:41:14,931
That reckless confidence
and strategy without solid reasoning

858
00:41:15,014 --> 00:41:20,144
could actually become a liability,
so I was happy ZZONE chose me.

859
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,397
[Jimin] Horseking.

860
00:41:24,399 --> 00:41:26,317
[Ddolddol] ZZONE picked Horseking first.

861
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:30,905
So I gave it a lot of thought.

862
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:35,243
I'll pick Yuk Junseo.

863
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:41,541
Who could go up against Horseking?

864
00:41:41,624 --> 00:41:43,710
So I chose Yuk Junseo.

865
00:41:43,793 --> 00:41:45,378
[dealer] Yuk Junseo has been selected.

866
00:41:45,461 --> 00:41:46,796
KIM DDOLDDOL PICKS YUK JUNSEO FIRST

867
00:41:47,714 --> 00:41:49,298
They're similar types.

868
00:41:49,382 --> 00:41:51,968
Physically strong players. [laughs]

869
00:41:52,051 --> 00:41:53,386
[ZZONE] Who should I pick?

870
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:54,679
Go with your instincts.

871
00:41:54,762 --> 00:41:58,224
You have to go with your gut.

872
00:41:59,976 --> 00:42:01,185
I'll pick...

873
00:42:03,646 --> 00:42:05,189
Yang Dail.

874
00:42:07,025 --> 00:42:08,026
[Ddolddol] What's happening?

875
00:42:08,109 --> 00:42:09,902
I really panicked at that moment.

876
00:42:09,986 --> 00:42:12,822
I thought, "Hold on,
what do I do now? I'm screwed."

877
00:42:13,448 --> 00:42:16,159
[Pani Bottle sighs] This is
driving me insane.

878
00:42:17,577 --> 00:42:20,621
When I heard that, I was irritated.

879
00:42:21,164 --> 00:42:25,460
[Jimin] I clearly told her the prison
members were our enemies.

880
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:27,086
How could she pick Yang Dail?

881
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:29,672
What's she even thinking?

882
00:42:29,756 --> 00:42:32,675
-Okay.
-[dealer] ZZONE has chosen Yang Dail.

883
00:42:32,759 --> 00:42:34,218
ZZONE PICKS YANG DAIL SECOND

884
00:42:34,302 --> 00:42:39,807
Dail seems like someone who stays calm
and won't lose his composure easily.

885
00:42:39,891 --> 00:42:42,852
I thought he'd make rational decisions
in critical moments.

886
00:42:42,935 --> 00:42:46,189
Also, I knew we needed
to break them apart eventually.

887
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:50,193
I was really happy watching them

888
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:52,487
get split apart one by one.

889
00:42:53,529 --> 00:42:56,032
[Dail] I'm not sure if she picked me
to separate me

890
00:42:56,115 --> 00:42:58,534
from Ddolddol and Pani Bottle.

891
00:42:58,618 --> 00:43:03,706
To me, the prison alliance
was meant to last until we left prison.

892
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:06,626
LAST NIGHT, JAEGYUN AND ZZONE WERE TALKING

893
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:08,795
DAIL NATURALLY JOINS THEM

894
00:43:08,878 --> 00:43:09,879
[Dail] What's that?

895
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:11,589
[ZZONE] We can see
after returning from prison.

896
00:43:11,672 --> 00:43:13,716
[Dail] I was so stressed out in there.

897
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:16,719
Personally,

898
00:43:16,803 --> 00:43:20,098
I know Pani Bottle
and Ddolddol aren't bad people.

899
00:43:20,181 --> 00:43:25,061
But if I'm around people like that,
I don't think I could stand it.

900
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,437
Because they're unpredictable?

901
00:43:26,521 --> 00:43:29,315
[Dail] If I'm with people
who might do something unpredictable,

902
00:43:29,398 --> 00:43:33,528
I'd have to keep an eye on them
all the time if we're on the same team.

903
00:43:33,611 --> 00:43:35,696
And that would stress me out.

904
00:43:35,780 --> 00:43:38,741
I got involved with Pani Bottle
in the first round

905
00:43:38,825 --> 00:43:40,409
and ended up being called "Mad Dail."

906
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:45,248
THE TWO CLASHED ON DAY ONE

907
00:43:45,331 --> 00:43:46,332
DURING TEAM SELECTION MEETING

908
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:47,416
If you win the draw...

909
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:49,043
-Us first?
-No, not us.

910
00:43:49,127 --> 00:43:50,419
Pick Yuk Junseo first.

911
00:43:50,503 --> 00:43:51,796
Then, you should pick Jaegyun.

912
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:53,047
DAIL MADE THEM NOT PICK HIM

913
00:43:53,131 --> 00:43:55,550
The alliance was only meant to last

914
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:59,637
until we got out of prison
and made it back into daylight.

915
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:03,432
Now, I can form a new team
and try to work well with them.

916
00:44:03,516 --> 00:44:06,227
No matter what team I'm on,
I'll play my hardest.

917
00:44:06,811 --> 00:44:09,021
Then, I'll go with Pani Bottle.

918
00:44:10,398 --> 00:44:11,482
Then, I can't give up.

919
00:44:11,566 --> 00:44:13,651
KIM DDOLDDOL PICKS PANI BOTTLE SECOND

920
00:44:14,235 --> 00:44:16,612
-It's not going to be easy.
-It'll be tough.

921
00:44:17,738 --> 00:44:19,073
Dail ended up there.

922
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:22,952
Pick Jaegyun, no matter what.

923
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,706
I'll pick Hwang Jaegyun.

924
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,293
[Ddolddol] What's her deal? It annoyed me.

925
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:33,212
-[dealer] ZZONE has chosen Hwang Jaegyun.
-[♪ tense synth music playing]

926
00:44:33,296 --> 00:44:34,797
ZZONE PICKS HWANG JAEGYUN THIRD

927
00:44:34,881 --> 00:44:38,551
I'll go with Jang Eunsil.

928
00:44:38,634 --> 00:44:40,928
[dealer] Kim Ddolddol
has chosen Jang Eunsil.

929
00:44:41,012 --> 00:44:42,430
KIM DDOLDDOL PICKS JANG EUNSIL THIRD

930
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:46,475
We don't have any choices left.
Whoever's left will join us.

931
00:44:47,226 --> 00:44:49,520
THE REMAINING PLAYERS
PARK JIMIN, LEE JOONSU

932
00:44:50,104 --> 00:44:54,275
Which one should we pick?

933
00:44:54,358 --> 00:44:56,485
[Horseking] We don't know
what game it'll be.

934
00:44:56,569 --> 00:44:57,904
[Jaegyun] Exactly. We don't know.

935
00:44:57,987 --> 00:44:59,363
We should bring Joonsu.

936
00:44:59,447 --> 00:45:01,908
If it's a physical game,
that'd be a good choice.

937
00:45:01,991 --> 00:45:05,494
-Joonsu is unexpectedly clever, right?
-ZZONE, please pick your last member.

938
00:45:05,578 --> 00:45:06,746
No, he's not very helpful.

939
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:08,372
Right, you have a point.

940
00:45:08,456 --> 00:45:10,041
He's not mentally tough.

941
00:45:10,166 --> 00:45:12,418
[Dail] I think that's really crucial.

942
00:45:12,501 --> 00:45:13,878
[Horseking sighs]

943
00:45:13,961 --> 00:45:18,174
[ZZONE] We were debating
because we wanted Joonsu for his strength,

944
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:22,553
but he might not be the right choice
when it comes to brains and politics.

945
00:45:22,637 --> 00:45:25,389
Jimin, on the other hand,
isn't physically strong,

946
00:45:25,473 --> 00:45:28,142
but she's strong with strategy.

947
00:45:28,809 --> 00:45:31,103
[Horseking] We might need someone
with more experience.

948
00:45:31,187 --> 00:45:32,271
[Dail] Then...

949
00:45:32,355 --> 00:45:33,856
They're taking their time.

950
00:45:33,940 --> 00:45:34,982
It's not a good feeling.

951
00:45:35,775 --> 00:45:36,776
It doesn't feel good.

952
00:45:37,985 --> 00:45:40,238
I've never been treated that way before

953
00:45:41,072 --> 00:45:44,533
in my entire life.

954
00:45:44,617 --> 00:45:46,994
I felt really hurt.

955
00:45:47,745 --> 00:45:51,207
[Joonsu] At first, I knew they could
take some time to talk it through,

956
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:53,584
but after five minutes went by,

957
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:54,835
I started getting annoyed.

958
00:45:54,919 --> 00:45:57,004
Is it really that hard to decide?

959
00:45:57,088 --> 00:45:58,339
Ugh...

960
00:45:58,881 --> 00:45:59,966
It's so hard.

961
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:04,637
I think we should go with this option.

962
00:46:05,805 --> 00:46:06,847
[Horseking] You think so?

963
00:46:08,140 --> 00:46:10,393
[ZZONE] I'll pick...

964
00:46:10,476 --> 00:46:12,353
[♪ music intensifies]

965
00:46:19,777 --> 00:46:21,779
Lee Joonsu.

966
00:46:21,862 --> 00:46:24,198
[dealer] ZZONE has chosen Lee Joonsu.

967
00:46:24,282 --> 00:46:25,491
ZZONE'S LAST PICK IS LEE JOONSU

968
00:46:28,953 --> 00:46:33,541
[Jimin sighs]
ZZONE didn't pick me in the end.

969
00:46:34,333 --> 00:46:38,337
After what happened with her,
I definitely felt betrayed by ZZONE.

970
00:46:38,421 --> 00:46:42,675
I wanted us to come together once
and prove that we could win.

971
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:44,510
I thought that would shift the whole game

972
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:46,804
and turn us into a team
that people would be wary of.

973
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:50,891
But ZZONE probably saw things differently.

974
00:46:50,975 --> 00:46:53,936
She seemed to make the choice

975
00:46:54,020 --> 00:46:56,188
that gave her
the best chance of surviving.

976
00:46:56,272 --> 00:46:59,859
And as a result,
many of the physically strong players

977
00:46:59,942 --> 00:47:02,194
ended up joining her side.

978
00:47:02,278 --> 00:47:04,113
I never wanted to be on that team,

979
00:47:04,196 --> 00:47:07,450
but I somehow ended up joining
Ddolddol's team.

980
00:47:07,533 --> 00:47:09,076
[dealer] Then automatically,

981
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:11,537
-Park Jimin will join Kim Ddolddol's team.
-Okay.

982
00:47:12,163 --> 00:47:13,164
[Ddolddol in English] Welcome.

983
00:47:14,623 --> 00:47:18,210
[Jimin in Korean] I was frustrated.
[sighs in exasperation]

984
00:47:18,294 --> 00:47:21,922
I started thinking that choosing ZZONE
as the leader was a mistake.

985
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:25,468
[ZZONE] I was torn until the last minute.

986
00:47:25,551 --> 00:47:29,221
My gut told me that teaming up with Jimin

987
00:47:29,305 --> 00:47:31,849
would have helped more strategically.

988
00:47:32,308 --> 00:47:33,309
[Horseking] What do you think?

989
00:47:33,392 --> 00:47:34,810
TEAM MEETING BEFORE FINAL SELECTION

990
00:47:34,894 --> 00:47:38,564
Pani Bottle and Jimin
aren't on good terms. [chuckles softly]

991
00:47:38,647 --> 00:47:39,648
[ZZONE] Ah, that's true.

992
00:47:40,399 --> 00:47:42,902
[Jaegyun] Putting them on the same team
could be a good move.

993
00:47:42,985 --> 00:47:47,239
[ZZONE] Jimin and Pani Bottle
don't like each other.

994
00:47:47,740 --> 00:47:48,824
[Jimin] Pani Bottle...

995
00:47:49,492 --> 00:47:50,743
I don't think we click at all.

996
00:47:50,826 --> 00:47:53,746
-[ZZONE] That's so funny.
-[Jimin] It'll be fucking hard to play

997
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:54,830
together with Pani Bottle.

998
00:47:54,914 --> 00:47:55,915
[ZZONE] Really?

999
00:47:55,998 --> 00:47:58,584
[Pani Bottle] We need to get rid
of Park Jimin eventually.

1000
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:00,753
I just don't like her.

1001
00:48:01,337 --> 00:48:03,839
She talked down and got mad at me
at the first Main Hall.

1002
00:48:03,923 --> 00:48:05,299
Since then, I've never liked her.

1003
00:48:05,383 --> 00:48:07,510
I can't fucking stand her.
This is a first.

1004
00:48:07,593 --> 00:48:09,011
JIMIN AND PANI BOTTLE DON'T GET ALONG

1005
00:48:09,095 --> 00:48:11,138
[ZZONE] These selected teams are crazy.

1006
00:48:11,764 --> 00:48:15,643
If we put Jimin and Pani Bottle together,

1007
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:18,687
our chances of winning
would be much higher.

1008
00:48:19,355 --> 00:48:21,982
After a lot of thought, I chose Joonsu.

1009
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:25,194
TEAM ZZONE
HORSEKING, DAIL, JAEGYUN, JOONSU

1010
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:27,363
TEAM DDOLDDOL
JUNSEO, PANI BOTTLE, EUNSIL, JIMIN

1011
00:48:27,988 --> 00:48:30,116
[mic feedback]

1012
00:48:30,199 --> 00:48:34,954
[host] We will now reveal
the third Main Match of Deadly Tag.

1013
00:48:36,705 --> 00:48:38,290
The third Main Match is...

1014
00:48:40,584 --> 00:48:42,294
"Kingmaker."

1015
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:43,379
"Kingmaker?"

1016
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:47,466
[host] "Kingmaker" is a game
where teams predict each other's ranks

1017
00:48:47,550 --> 00:48:52,138
and go through card battles
to eliminate the opposing team's cards.

1018
00:48:52,930 --> 00:48:57,935
Each team chooses
one of two bases on the game area.

1019
00:48:58,018 --> 00:49:01,230
Before the game begins,
each team will hold a discussion

1020
00:49:01,313 --> 00:49:05,401
and distribute a total of 11 rank cards
among its members.

1021
00:49:06,235 --> 00:49:09,405
The deck consists of one King,
the highest-ranking card,

1022
00:49:09,488 --> 00:49:12,199
nine numbered cards,

1023
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:15,953
and one Joker, the lowest-ranking card.

1024
00:49:17,705 --> 00:49:20,458
The higher the number,
the stronger the card.

1025
00:49:20,541 --> 00:49:23,419
The King card beats every other card.

1026
00:49:24,587 --> 00:49:29,258
However, the King card loses to the Joker,
the lowest-ranking card.

1027
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:33,262
-So only the Joker can beat the King.
-Right.

1028
00:49:33,345 --> 00:49:35,264
-And the 1 beats the Joker?
-That's right.

1029
00:49:35,347 --> 00:49:37,725
The Joker can't beat any card
except the King.

1030
00:49:37,808 --> 00:49:41,020
[host] Each player receives
two rank cards,

1031
00:49:41,103 --> 00:49:44,356
while the player holding the Joker
receives three cards.

1032
00:49:45,274 --> 00:49:50,196
However, the King and the Joker
cannot be held by the same player.

1033
00:49:51,447 --> 00:49:55,659
Players are not allowed to transfer
or exchange cards during the game.

1034
00:49:56,911 --> 00:50:01,123
"Kingmaker" consists of two phases,
the Battle Round and the Strategy Round.

1035
00:50:01,874 --> 00:50:03,459
Once the Battle Round begins,

1036
00:50:03,542 --> 00:50:05,753
players can tag members
of the opposing team.

1037
00:50:06,420 --> 00:50:10,549
When a tag occurs, the two players
will move to the nearest Dealer Room

1038
00:50:10,633 --> 00:50:12,426
to conduct a card battle.

1039
00:50:13,844 --> 00:50:17,264
In a card battle,
each player secretly hands

1040
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:19,141
one card to the dealer.

1041
00:50:19,975 --> 00:50:22,895
The winning card is removed from play,

1042
00:50:22,978 --> 00:50:25,314
and the winner takes
the losing player's card.

1043
00:50:27,107 --> 00:50:30,444
If you win with the King card,
you get to keep the King card.

1044
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:35,074
If both players reveal cards
of the same rank, nothing happens.

1045
00:50:35,783 --> 00:50:38,827
Any player who runs out of rank cards

1046
00:50:38,911 --> 00:50:40,996
is immediately removed from the game.

1047
00:50:41,664 --> 00:50:42,790
Gosh, that's brutal.

1048
00:50:44,208 --> 00:50:47,836
[host] After each Battle Round,
there is a five-minute Strategy Round.

1049
00:50:47,920 --> 00:50:51,131
Once those five minutes end,
another Battle Round begins.

1050
00:50:51,215 --> 00:50:56,220
This cycle continues until one team
captures the opposing team's King card.

1051
00:50:56,303 --> 00:50:58,305
The first team to do so wins.

1052
00:51:00,391 --> 00:51:02,810
This has nothing to do
with physical strength.

1053
00:51:02,893 --> 00:51:04,353
It's all about using your brain.

1054
00:51:05,145 --> 00:51:06,146
[sighs]

1055
00:51:06,647 --> 00:51:11,569
[host] In addition,
each team has 15 symbols.

1056
00:51:12,486 --> 00:51:13,821
What? Symbols?

1057
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:18,117
Teams must protect their own symbols
while stealing the opposition's symbols.

1058
00:51:19,118 --> 00:51:23,080
The number of symbols captured
determines the advantages the team earns.

1059
00:51:23,914 --> 00:51:25,332
Oh...

1060
00:51:26,125 --> 00:51:29,169
Symbols... We need to capture them.

1061
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:31,171
While playing the card game?

1062
00:51:31,797 --> 00:51:35,259
The symbols are important and all,
but there's no need to focus on them.

1063
00:51:35,342 --> 00:51:36,844
-Let's win the card battles...
-[Jimin] Right.

1064
00:51:36,927 --> 00:51:38,804
...and take out all the opposing players.

1065
00:51:38,887 --> 00:51:39,972
[Jimin] The Joker is the key.

1066
00:51:40,055 --> 00:51:42,057
-Once you take the King, it's over.
-Exactly.

1067
00:51:42,141 --> 00:51:45,227
You chase each other's tails
and end up back where you started.

1068
00:51:45,311 --> 00:51:48,439
This is basically a complicated game
of rock, paper, scissors.

1069
00:51:48,522 --> 00:51:49,982
Since it's a card game,

1070
00:51:50,065 --> 00:51:52,109
I thought using our brains
would be important.

1071
00:51:52,192 --> 00:51:56,947
We need to decide right now
who will take King and Joker cards.

1072
00:51:57,031 --> 00:51:58,616
Do we give it to someone fast

1073
00:51:58,699 --> 00:52:00,826
or someone who looks like an easy target

1074
00:52:00,909 --> 00:52:03,370
-and make it a battle of wits?
-[ZZONE] A battle of wits.

1075
00:52:03,454 --> 00:52:06,290
Before anything else,
what do you think they'll give Junseo?

1076
00:52:07,082 --> 00:52:09,251
-I think he'll get the King.
-[Dail] You think so?

1077
00:52:10,711 --> 00:52:13,172
Why do I feel like
they won't give Junseo the King?

1078
00:52:13,255 --> 00:52:16,342
We'll need to use our heads
more than we think in this game.

1079
00:52:16,425 --> 00:52:19,178
When Junseo becomes absorbed,
he stops thinking logically.

1080
00:52:19,261 --> 00:52:21,680
You need to keep your cool
in this card game.

1081
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:25,017
They'd never give the King to someone
who loses their composure.

1082
00:52:25,100 --> 00:52:27,895
I think they'll give him
an 8 or 9 instead.

1083
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:30,898
Instead of taking some weak card

1084
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:34,568
and risking having it stolen,
I'd rather give Junseo an 8 or 9.

1085
00:52:34,652 --> 00:52:36,028
Then, Junseo needs

1086
00:52:36,111 --> 00:52:38,906
to keep dodging everyone like hell
as if he has the King.

1087
00:52:38,989 --> 00:52:43,160
You know that thing you do when your eyes
turn red and you run like mad?

1088
00:52:43,243 --> 00:52:44,620
That should be enough.

1089
00:52:44,703 --> 00:52:47,081
Take an 8 or 9, act fucking cocky
as if you're the King.

1090
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:48,248
-"Cocky."
-That's fucking funny.

1091
00:52:48,332 --> 00:52:50,334
Then, take the Joker later on
and beat the King.

1092
00:52:50,417 --> 00:52:51,835
-You'll be the hero.
-That's so cool.

1093
00:52:51,919 --> 00:52:53,295
[Ddolddol] That's going to be so cool.

1094
00:52:53,379 --> 00:52:55,339
-Let's make him the real King.
-[Jimin] That's so cool.

1095
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:59,760
Once we identify who their King is,
we'll have to chase them down to tag them.

1096
00:52:59,843 --> 00:53:02,429
So they're going to give
the Joker and the King

1097
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:04,723
to someone who's athletic or fast.

1098
00:53:04,807 --> 00:53:05,891
Jaegyun or Horseking.

1099
00:53:05,974 --> 00:53:07,643
-I think it'll be one of the two.
-Yes.

1100
00:53:07,726 --> 00:53:09,937
But that's a little too one-dimensional.

1101
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:12,272
Fast people get the King or the Joker.

1102
00:53:12,356 --> 00:53:14,608
-Isn't that obvious?
-There's a reason.

1103
00:53:14,692 --> 00:53:17,194
To catch the King with the Joker,
you have to run fast.

1104
00:53:17,277 --> 00:53:19,613
-Fast runners can catch up.
-But think about this.

1105
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:22,991
If we work together
to keep chasing Horseking,

1106
00:53:23,575 --> 00:53:25,452
when he's exhausted, you can tag him.

1107
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:26,620
-So I think...
-Right.

1108
00:53:26,704 --> 00:53:28,872
If we coordinate, we can still catch them.

1109
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:32,167
[Pani Bottle] Being fast
gives us more options.

1110
00:53:32,251 --> 00:53:33,961
We can choose
when we want to fight or not.

1111
00:53:34,044 --> 00:53:35,254
PANI BOTTLE DISAGREES WITH JIMIN

1112
00:53:35,337 --> 00:53:37,005
If that's not an option,

1113
00:53:37,089 --> 00:53:40,050
we need to think about
whether we need to give a key role

1114
00:53:40,134 --> 00:53:41,760
to someone who doesn't run well.

1115
00:53:41,844 --> 00:53:43,804
[Jimin] Don't you think
they might try to tag me

1116
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:45,848
since it'll seem like I have weaker cards?

1117
00:53:47,141 --> 00:53:49,601
Or wouldn't it be better
if I beat everyone as the King?

1118
00:53:49,685 --> 00:53:51,645
JIMIN REFUSES TO BACK DOWN

1119
00:53:51,729 --> 00:53:54,273
When I heard that, I thought,
"What's her deal?"

1120
00:53:54,857 --> 00:53:58,068
I had no idea what to make of her.
Something about her is so weird.

1121
00:53:58,652 --> 00:54:00,821
I had the Seeker mission.

1122
00:54:00,904 --> 00:54:03,031
[sighs in exasperation]
This is driving me crazy.

1123
00:54:04,366 --> 00:54:08,036
The mission was to compete against
the opposing team at least three times.

1124
00:54:08,120 --> 00:54:13,876
The Joker was a card that would let me
play three times, no matter what.

1125
00:54:13,959 --> 00:54:16,128
There was a high chance
of beating the King.

1126
00:54:16,211 --> 00:54:18,505
The King and the Joker
were perfect for me.

1127
00:54:18,589 --> 00:54:20,799
You need to win the battle of wits too.

1128
00:54:20,883 --> 00:54:22,176
If you have the King and 6,

1129
00:54:22,259 --> 00:54:23,761
you need to read the opponent

1130
00:54:23,844 --> 00:54:25,179
-to play the 6 correctly.
-[Ddolddol] Right.

1131
00:54:25,262 --> 00:54:26,388
JIMIN APPEALS FOR KING OR JOKER

1132
00:54:26,472 --> 00:54:27,514
Are you good?

1133
00:54:28,390 --> 00:54:32,644
I tried to convince our leader
that I can bluff convincingly.

1134
00:54:32,728 --> 00:54:35,230
Since the timing
of when you play a card is crucial,

1135
00:54:35,314 --> 00:54:36,940
I thought the King and the Joker

1136
00:54:37,024 --> 00:54:40,194
should go to people
who are strong in a battle of wits.

1137
00:54:40,277 --> 00:54:42,696
It wouldn't be a bad idea if Jimin did it.

1138
00:54:42,780 --> 00:54:44,114
Or are those roles too important?

1139
00:54:44,198 --> 00:54:46,283
It's kind of risky.

1140
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:52,414
Let's narrow it down to two for now
and decide tomorrow.

1141
00:54:52,498 --> 00:54:55,083
If we don't settle it,
we'll repeat this tomorrow.

1142
00:54:55,167 --> 00:54:57,544
[Jimin] We'll talk about it tomorrow.
Sleep tight.

1143
00:54:57,628 --> 00:54:58,629
[Ddolddol] I'm so tired.

1144
00:55:00,797 --> 00:55:04,051
[Pani Bottle sighs] I'm against
giving the King to Park Jimin.

1145
00:55:04,134 --> 00:55:05,802
Me too. I can't really trust her.

1146
00:55:05,886 --> 00:55:10,516
If we fail, we'll end up
in the Death Match. It's too risky.

1147
00:55:11,099 --> 00:55:13,560
-What should we give to Jimin?
-[♪ contemplative music playing]

1148
00:55:13,644 --> 00:55:16,313
It's too risky
to give a crucial card to her.

1149
00:55:17,022 --> 00:55:21,068
We should rule out giving the King
or the Joker to anyone who isn't fast.

1150
00:55:21,151 --> 00:55:22,611
I'm completely against it.

1151
00:55:26,114 --> 00:55:29,910
[♪ ominous music playing]

1152
00:55:29,993 --> 00:55:31,453
[crows cawing]

1153
00:55:31,537 --> 00:55:33,413
[Ddolddol] Oh my, what are these reeds?

1154
00:55:38,335 --> 00:55:40,379
[ZZONE] Wait, this is an actual school.

1155
00:55:43,382 --> 00:55:45,509
[♪ rock music playing]

1156
00:55:51,348 --> 00:55:55,352
[Jaegyun] Any player I considered
a threat? There was no one among them.

1157
00:55:56,395 --> 00:55:59,439
[Dail] I honestly think I'm not someone
people can easily take down.

1158
00:56:00,816 --> 00:56:02,818
[Horseking] I'll show you
what a real team is like

1159
00:56:02,901 --> 00:56:06,613
and how big of a role I'll play.

1160
00:56:10,826 --> 00:56:12,160
[Ddolddol] Just at a glance,

1161
00:56:12,244 --> 00:56:14,454
they're a cute girl with pink hair
and four big dudes.

1162
00:56:15,664 --> 00:56:18,250
They don't look like much.
Our team will beat them.

1163
00:56:19,751 --> 00:56:23,797
[Junseo] I'm someone who hates losing,
and I absolutely refuse to lose.

1164
00:56:24,506 --> 00:56:27,634
[Eunsil] Our entire team
is fired up right now.

1165
00:56:27,718 --> 00:56:29,720
I believe we can crush them.

1166
00:56:37,519 --> 00:56:38,687
[mic feedback]

1167
00:56:39,855 --> 00:56:42,941
[host] We will explain the Kingmaker area
and the symbols.

1168
00:56:43,609 --> 00:56:47,571
The "Kingmaker" area consists
of the Red Team Base, Blue Team Base,

1169
00:56:48,196 --> 00:56:50,115
and the Neutral Zone.

1170
00:56:50,866 --> 00:56:53,702
Each team has 15 symbols in total.

1171
00:56:54,286 --> 00:56:56,872
Eight are hidden in each base,

1172
00:56:56,955 --> 00:57:00,042
and seven are hidden in the Neutral Zone.

1173
00:57:00,125 --> 00:57:03,045
Shouldn't we start with the Neutral Zone
and win that area?

1174
00:57:03,128 --> 00:57:04,504
It might be worth quickly searching

1175
00:57:04,588 --> 00:57:06,298
-the Neutral Zone.
-There are seven there.

1176
00:57:06,381 --> 00:57:08,258
[host] Each base has a map

1177
00:57:08,342 --> 00:57:10,969
showing 14 locations
marked by their team symbol,

1178
00:57:11,053 --> 00:57:13,555
while one location remains undisclosed.

1179
00:57:13,639 --> 00:57:16,767
Players must find and secure
the opposing team's symbols,

1180
00:57:17,225 --> 00:57:19,436
bring them back to the Dealer Room
in their own base,

1181
00:57:19,519 --> 00:57:21,271
and destroy the symbols.

1182
00:57:21,938 --> 00:57:23,815
Once a team captures four symbols,

1183
00:57:23,899 --> 00:57:27,736
the player holding the opposing team's
4 card will be revealed.

1184
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:33,241
If the 4 card has already been taken out,
the next higher card will be revealed.

1185
00:57:33,325 --> 00:57:36,912
Once a team captures seven symbols,
they will obtain a Shuffle Ticket.

1186
00:57:37,454 --> 00:57:38,789
A Shuffle Ticket allows a player

1187
00:57:38,872 --> 00:57:43,335
to exchange one card
that is not the King with a teammate.

1188
00:57:43,418 --> 00:57:45,212
Once a team retrieves 10 symbols,

1189
00:57:45,295 --> 00:57:48,674
the opposing team's highest-ranking card
that is not the King card

1190
00:57:48,757 --> 00:57:49,758
can be eliminated.

1191
00:57:51,343 --> 00:57:55,305
Once we find four symbols,
we can start crushing them.

1192
00:57:55,389 --> 00:57:58,225
[Pani Bottle] If both sides go,
"Let's tag everyone and end this,"

1193
00:57:58,308 --> 00:57:59,685
then the symbols won't matter.

1194
00:57:59,768 --> 00:58:01,144
That's not how it'll go at first.

1195
00:58:01,228 --> 00:58:03,188
We'll all size each other up,
so symbols matter.

1196
00:58:03,271 --> 00:58:04,356
It's a huge variable.

1197
00:58:04,439 --> 00:58:07,818
[host] You will now explore the bases.

1198
00:58:07,901 --> 00:58:10,153
BLUE TEAM BASE

1199
00:58:10,237 --> 00:58:11,530
[Ddolddol] It's so big.

1200
00:58:11,613 --> 00:58:13,240
[Junseo] It's bigger than expected.

1201
00:58:13,323 --> 00:58:15,492
DEALER ROOM ON FAR RIGHT SIDE
OF MAIN ENTRANCE

1202
00:58:15,575 --> 00:58:17,452
[Ddolddol] I guess
we smash them with a hammer.

1203
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:19,621
[ZZONE] It'll be hard to find symbols.

1204
00:58:19,705 --> 00:58:20,747
SPACIOUS BLUE TEAM BASE

1205
00:58:20,831 --> 00:58:22,416
[Dail] This will be good for hiding.

1206
00:58:22,499 --> 00:58:24,084
[ZZONE] It seems like
a good defensive spot.

1207
00:58:24,167 --> 00:58:26,628
No, if you hide,
it allows the other team to attack more.

1208
00:58:26,712 --> 00:58:27,713
[Ddolddol] In the professor's office,

1209
00:58:27,796 --> 00:58:29,297
-there's an opening.
-[Junseo] There's a hole.

1210
00:58:29,381 --> 00:58:30,507
KIM DDOLDDOL

1211
00:58:30,590 --> 00:58:31,925
[ZZONE] Doesn't it feel too empty?

1212
00:58:32,008 --> 00:58:34,469
It's basically impossible to sneak into.

1213
00:58:34,553 --> 00:58:40,350
[Dail] It's so wide open
that if someone tries to sneak in,

1214
00:58:40,434 --> 00:58:44,563
we could miss them
if we drop our guard even for a second.

1215
00:58:44,646 --> 00:58:46,565
It feels like we'd get completely exposed.

1216
00:58:46,940 --> 00:58:49,025
RED TEAM BASE

1217
00:58:49,109 --> 00:58:53,071
To stay defensive and dodge them,
this place is way better.

1218
00:58:54,239 --> 00:58:56,032
RED TEAM BASE IS FILLED WITH OBSTACLES

1219
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:59,202
[Dail] We have to open each one?
There has to be a symbol here.

1220
00:58:59,286 --> 00:59:02,789
[ZZONE] Right, Horseking will need
to show us some parkour.

1221
00:59:02,873 --> 00:59:04,666
-[Ddolddol] What is this place?
-[Junseo] Board games?

1222
00:59:04,750 --> 00:59:06,835
[Ddolddol] Something about this
feels suspicious.

1223
00:59:06,918 --> 00:59:09,212
-It feels like a Death Match area.
-[Junseo] Right.

1224
00:59:09,296 --> 00:59:11,465
The inside felt complicated.

1225
00:59:11,548 --> 00:59:17,471
There were much more obstacles
on the way in than the Blue Team Base,

1226
00:59:17,554 --> 00:59:19,681
so it might be better
for hiding and defense.

1227
00:59:19,765 --> 00:59:21,725
This leads to the Neutral Zone.

1228
00:59:21,808 --> 00:59:23,226
[Ddolddol] When we go this way,

1229
00:59:23,310 --> 00:59:24,686
-it goes like this.
-[Junseo] Right.

1230
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:27,230
It's much more closer to the Neutral Zone.

1231
00:59:28,190 --> 00:59:29,941
PARKING LOT

1232
00:59:30,025 --> 00:59:31,902
REED FIELD

1233
00:59:31,985 --> 00:59:35,489
NEUTRAL ZONE
13,112 SQUARE METERS (4,000 PYEONG)

1234
00:59:35,572 --> 00:59:38,700
Well, at first glance,

1235
00:59:38,784 --> 00:59:41,912
the Red Team Base feels
a lot narrower overall.

1236
00:59:41,995 --> 00:59:43,205
This one's bigger.

1237
00:59:43,288 --> 00:59:44,289
The pros and cons are clear.

1238
00:59:44,581 --> 00:59:46,374
-[Dail] Right.
-That place is very closed off.

1239
00:59:46,458 --> 00:59:47,667
-[Dail] It's enclosed.
-[ZZONE] It's narrow...

1240
00:59:47,751 --> 00:59:49,044
"RED TEAM BASE"

1241
00:59:49,127 --> 00:59:50,253
-...and packed with objects.
-[Dail] Yes.

1242
00:59:50,337 --> 00:59:52,255
You have to dig around a lot.
This is much bigger.

1243
00:59:52,339 --> 00:59:53,340
BLUE TEAM BASE

1244
00:59:53,423 --> 00:59:55,425
-[Dail] A lot of hiding spots.
-[Joonsu] There are four entrances.

1245
00:59:55,509 --> 00:59:57,511
[Horseking] The Red Team Base
is easier for defense?

1246
00:59:57,594 --> 00:59:59,262
-[Dail] It's narrower.
-[Horseking] Ah.

1247
00:59:59,346 --> 01:00:03,809
If you try to take symbols from there,
it'll be a lot easier to get tagged.

1248
01:00:03,892 --> 01:00:06,144
-[ZZONE] Right.
-Because the entrance is narrow.

1249
01:00:06,228 --> 01:00:09,689
Since the Red Team Base
is much smaller than Blue's,

1250
01:00:09,773 --> 01:00:11,858
it's way easier to defend.

1251
01:00:12,484 --> 01:00:14,444
[mic feedback]

1252
01:00:14,986 --> 01:00:17,864
[host] It's time to choose the team bases.

1253
01:00:17,948 --> 01:00:22,118
Team Kim Ddolddol has the higher total
of personal funds,

1254
01:00:22,202 --> 01:00:25,038
so they get first choice.

1255
01:00:25,831 --> 01:00:27,123
All right.

1256
01:00:28,792 --> 01:00:31,294
We'll choose the Red Team Base
as our home base.

1257
01:00:32,462 --> 01:00:34,923
[Dail] Hmm, I was really disappointed.

1258
01:00:35,006 --> 01:00:38,844
We didn't have the option of choosing
our base, so it is what it is.

1259
01:00:38,927 --> 01:00:43,014
[host] Both teams, head to your bases
and begin your strategy meeting.

1260
01:00:43,807 --> 01:00:46,518
[Junseo] Feels like they'll go with
the standard game plan.

1261
01:00:46,601 --> 01:00:47,894
-[Ddolddol] Right?
-[Junseo] Yes.

1262
01:00:47,978 --> 01:00:50,397
I have a feeling
one of their fastest players

1263
01:00:50,480 --> 01:00:52,357
is holding the King.

1264
01:00:52,440 --> 01:00:53,441
I agree with that.

1265
01:00:53,525 --> 01:00:57,904
[Ddolddol] I think the King should be
among Yang Dail, Horseking, and Jaegyun.

1266
01:00:57,988 --> 01:00:58,989
I bet Junseo and Eunsil

1267
01:00:59,072 --> 01:01:00,907
-each have a high-ranking card.
-Yeah.

1268
01:01:00,991 --> 01:01:03,994
As for Eunsil, it's best
to have the King tag her.

1269
01:01:04,077 --> 01:01:05,161
-I bet Eunsil...
-[Jaegyun] Never.

1270
01:01:05,245 --> 01:01:07,873
-...doesn't have one.
-[Dail] They'd never give her the King.

1271
01:01:07,956 --> 01:01:09,749
Who do you think has the Joker?

1272
01:01:09,833 --> 01:01:13,545
Joker and King are probably
with players who are either fast

1273
01:01:13,628 --> 01:01:16,172
or completely off the radar.
That's most likely.

1274
01:01:16,256 --> 01:01:17,549
The King has to be played

1275
01:01:17,632 --> 01:01:18,633
-aggressively.
-Yes.

1276
01:01:18,717 --> 01:01:20,010
The odds are Junseo has it.

1277
01:01:20,093 --> 01:01:22,012
The most likely person is Junseo too.

1278
01:01:22,095 --> 01:01:23,388
It has to be Yuk Junseo.

1279
01:01:23,471 --> 01:01:26,224
Yuk Junseo had to be the one
holding the King.

1280
01:01:26,308 --> 01:01:27,809
Or someone brilliant.

1281
01:01:28,894 --> 01:01:32,439
But I don't think they have anyone
who's really brilliant.

1282
01:01:33,106 --> 01:01:35,650
You should play aggressively, Junseo.

1283
01:01:35,734 --> 01:01:36,902
-Okay.
-Pretend to be the King.

1284
01:01:36,985 --> 01:01:38,737
Junseo should go all out and wild.

1285
01:01:38,820 --> 01:01:40,280
-[Ddolddol] It's a bluff.
-I'll take this first.

1286
01:01:40,363 --> 01:01:43,825
BLUE TEAM'S GUESS
YUK JUNSEO

1287
01:01:43,909 --> 01:01:45,076
I'll just be the King.

1288
01:01:45,160 --> 01:01:47,329
They'll probably go,
"The leader can't be the King."

1289
01:01:47,412 --> 01:01:48,914
They'll probably assume

1290
01:01:48,997 --> 01:01:50,165
-I was given the Joker.
-[Pani Bottle] Right.

1291
01:01:50,248 --> 01:01:51,249
KIM DDOLDDOL

1292
01:01:51,333 --> 01:01:54,294
The King has to be fast,
but they also need to win mind games.

1293
01:01:54,377 --> 01:01:56,838
So I thought he'd be suited for the King.

1294
01:01:56,922 --> 01:02:00,091
[Ddolddol] They're definitely expecting
Eunsil to charge in aggressively.

1295
01:02:00,175 --> 01:02:02,928
So we could give the Joker to Eunsil
and then move it to Jimin.

1296
01:02:03,011 --> 01:02:07,098
Or we could give Jimin the Joker
and if the King happens to...

1297
01:02:07,182 --> 01:02:10,101
They already have a certain image of me,

1298
01:02:10,185 --> 01:02:12,562
so they'll assume
I'm just a throwaway card.

1299
01:02:12,646 --> 01:02:14,189
I wanted to get the Joker.

1300
01:02:14,272 --> 01:02:15,774
Think outside the box.

1301
01:02:15,857 --> 01:02:20,820
The card should go to someone
nobody would expect,

1302
01:02:20,904 --> 01:02:22,822
so the other team can't predict it.

1303
01:02:22,906 --> 01:02:24,991
WHO HAS THE JOKER ON THE RED TEAM?

1304
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:29,454
[Jaegyun] So Horseking
is definitely taking that [bleep], right?

1305
01:02:29,537 --> 01:02:30,664
[all] Yes.

1306
01:02:30,747 --> 01:02:32,123
[Dail] I'll take the 8 card.

1307
01:02:32,832 --> 01:02:33,917
[Jaegyun] Then, I'll take [bleep].

1308
01:02:34,417 --> 01:02:36,836
I'm sure I'll get caught,
so I should take a lower number.

1309
01:02:36,920 --> 01:02:38,713
[Jaegyun] So your role
is to keep bluffing.

1310
01:02:38,797 --> 01:02:39,881
Keep these two hidden

1311
01:02:39,965 --> 01:02:41,383
-as much as possible.
-[ZZONE] Okay.

1312
01:02:42,300 --> 01:02:44,219
[Jaegyun] So we're set on these numbers?

1313
01:02:44,719 --> 01:02:46,596
[Horseking] Yes. We can't change it now.

1314
01:02:46,680 --> 01:02:49,307
-This should be our cheat code.
-[ZZONE] I bet they won't expect this.

1315
01:02:49,391 --> 01:02:54,312
KIM DDOLDDOL, YUK JUNSEO, PANI BOTTLE,
JANG EUNSIL, PARK JIMIN

1316
01:02:54,396 --> 01:02:59,317
ZZONE, HORSEKING, YANG DAIL,
HWANG JAEGYUN, LEE JOONSU

1317
01:02:59,401 --> 01:03:01,736
[rustling]

1318
01:03:07,867 --> 01:03:12,080
[host] The "Kingmaker" Battle Round
starts now.

1319
01:03:12,163 --> 01:03:13,331
-[Horseking in English] Let's go.
-[Jaegyun in Korean] Let's go.

1320
01:03:13,415 --> 01:03:14,416
[ZZONE] Way to go!

1321
01:03:14,499 --> 01:03:16,251
[Horseking] You have to put on an act.

1322
01:03:16,334 --> 01:03:18,503
-[ZZONE laughs]
-[Joonsu] This will be fun as hell.

1323
01:03:20,046 --> 01:03:21,131
Follow me, follow me.

1324
01:03:21,214 --> 01:03:22,674
-[Junseo] Did you bring the notebook?
-[Ddolddol] Yes.

1325
01:03:24,467 --> 01:03:26,094
-[Eunsil] Search first?
-[Ddolddol] Yeah, search first.

1326
01:03:28,888 --> 01:03:29,889
There they are.

1327
01:03:31,683 --> 01:03:33,560
-They're running over.
-[Horseking] They're coming together.

1328
01:03:33,643 --> 01:03:35,729
-[ZZONE] They're running over.
-[Horseking] They're coming as a group.

1329
01:03:35,812 --> 01:03:37,313
-[Ddolddol] Go to the right.
-[Pani Bottle] To the right?

1330
01:03:37,397 --> 01:03:38,606
[Ddolddol] Go right and to the side door.

1331
01:03:38,690 --> 01:03:40,358
RED TEAM RUSHES IN RIGHT AWAY

1332
01:03:40,442 --> 01:03:42,277
-[Horseking] Dail! Dail!
-[ZZONE] They're coming.

1333
01:03:42,360 --> 01:03:43,403
-[Joonsu] Horseking!
-[Jaegyun] Dail!

1334
01:03:43,486 --> 01:03:45,196
They're all coming together!

1335
01:03:45,280 --> 01:03:46,948
I thought, "What are they doing?"

1336
01:03:47,032 --> 01:03:52,662
The five of them were all coming in
like some morning running crew.

1337
01:03:52,746 --> 01:03:57,250
Even when we were facing each other,
they ignored me like I was invisible.

1338
01:03:57,333 --> 01:03:58,376
Hang on!

1339
01:04:00,170 --> 01:04:01,212
[ZZONE laughs] What kind
of strategy is this?

1340
01:04:01,296 --> 01:04:02,630
GOING STRAIGHT AND IGNORING BLUE TEAM

1341
01:04:03,381 --> 01:04:06,801
I was so startled. I thought they were
coming in to tag someone.

1342
01:04:14,100 --> 01:04:17,479
THEY ENTER BLUE TEAM BASE IN AN INSTANT

1343
01:04:17,562 --> 01:04:19,814
[panting]

1344
01:04:22,025 --> 01:04:23,651
[Junseo] The Red Team's plan at the start

1345
01:04:23,735 --> 01:04:26,446
was to move together
and play aggressively.

1346
01:04:27,072 --> 01:04:30,658
We planned to look for the symbols boldly,
as if everyone was the King.

1347
01:04:32,160 --> 01:04:36,081
FOUND A SYMBOL

1348
01:04:36,164 --> 01:04:38,333
[♪ rock music playing]

1349
01:04:38,416 --> 01:04:39,793
[Ddolddol] Okay.

1350
01:04:39,918 --> 01:04:40,919
Let's go.

1351
01:04:41,795 --> 01:04:43,505
SYMBOLS CAN ONLY BE BROKEN
AT YOUR OWN BASE

1352
01:04:43,588 --> 01:04:44,923
[Jimin] I'll take from here.

1353
01:04:47,008 --> 01:04:49,177
[Pani Bottle] Pass it to me.

1354
01:04:49,260 --> 01:04:52,597
MOVING SYMBOL TO THE RED TEAM BASE

1355
01:04:53,389 --> 01:04:54,933
[Horseking] Over there! He's taking one!

1356
01:04:55,809 --> 01:04:59,395
RED TEAM BASE DEALER ROOM

1357
01:05:01,564 --> 01:05:02,565
RED TEAM DESTROYS ONE SYMBOL

1358
01:05:08,530 --> 01:05:09,697
[alarm blaring]

1359
01:05:10,824 --> 01:05:12,450
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Tag?

1360
01:05:12,534 --> 01:05:13,618
Fuck, who is it?

1361
01:05:13,701 --> 01:05:18,206
[host] All other players,
please return to your team's base.

1362
01:05:18,289 --> 01:05:20,542
What the heck? Who is it?

1363
01:05:22,127 --> 01:05:23,962
FIRST TAG

1364
01:05:24,045 --> 01:05:27,382
HORSEKING

1365
01:05:27,465 --> 01:05:30,301
JANG EUNSIL

1366
01:05:30,844 --> 01:05:32,595
[Horseking] Wait! Over there!
He's taking one!

1367
01:05:32,679 --> 01:05:34,389
LOST SYMBOL TOO EASILY
TO SURPRISE ATTACK

1368
01:05:34,472 --> 01:05:37,267
I didn't know what was going on at first.

1369
01:05:37,350 --> 01:05:40,145
In any case,
I wanted to leave them with one card.

1370
01:05:40,228 --> 01:05:41,229
So...

1371
01:05:41,312 --> 01:05:42,856
RED TEAM KEEPS IGNORING BLUE TEAM

1372
01:05:43,606 --> 01:05:44,607
-Tag.
-[alarm blaring]

1373
01:05:44,691 --> 01:05:45,900
HORSEKING TAGS EUNSIL

1374
01:05:45,984 --> 01:05:47,443
[host] Tag confirmed.

1375
01:05:48,153 --> 01:05:49,737
If you tagged me, we should go.

1376
01:05:50,280 --> 01:05:52,157
[Horseking] But she was so confident.

1377
01:05:52,824 --> 01:05:56,828
I was really thrown off and confused,
I wondered, "What is going on?"

1378
01:05:57,328 --> 01:05:59,622
Where does she get the nerve? How?

1379
01:06:02,709 --> 01:06:04,752
[dealer] Both players,
please submit your cards.

1380
01:06:04,836 --> 01:06:05,920
[Horseking exhales sharply]

1381
01:06:06,337 --> 01:06:08,256
HORSEKING AND EUNSIL HAND IN THEIR CARDS

1382
01:06:09,090 --> 01:06:10,091
UNFAZED

1383
01:06:10,175 --> 01:06:11,176
[Horseking] What is this strategy?

1384
01:06:11,259 --> 01:06:12,969
[dealer] We will check the cards.

1385
01:06:13,052 --> 01:06:16,097
JANG EUNSIL, HORSEKING

1386
01:06:16,181 --> 01:06:20,143
[Eunsil] The 7 was a high card,
so I thought I could beat him.

1387
01:06:20,226 --> 01:06:22,604
Horseking? Why would he tag Eunsil?

1388
01:06:22,687 --> 01:06:24,439
RED TEAM IS CONVINCED THEY'LL WIN

1389
01:06:24,522 --> 01:06:25,523
Why did he tag her?

1390
01:06:26,399 --> 01:06:27,859
He's going to regret it.

1391
01:06:28,484 --> 01:06:30,612
Let's check our phones.

1392
01:06:32,864 --> 01:06:36,409
Her 7 lost to Horseking. Eunsil lost.

1393
01:06:36,492 --> 01:06:37,785
EUNSIL
I LOST TO HORSEKING WITH A 7

1394
01:06:37,869 --> 01:06:40,079
[dealer] Horseking has won.

1395
01:06:45,627 --> 01:06:49,047
JANG EUNSIL'S 7 CARD IS ELIMINATED

1396
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:53,218
SIGH

1397
01:06:55,053 --> 01:06:56,095
Maybe Horseking has the King.

1398
01:06:56,179 --> 01:06:59,599
I don't think Horseking is the King.
The King would be lying low.

1399
01:06:59,682 --> 01:07:01,935
-I think he has a 9.
-[Pani Bottle] Could this be real?

1400
01:07:02,018 --> 01:07:05,396
This is really confusing.
It says Horseking has a 9.

1401
01:07:05,480 --> 01:07:07,565
-What is this?
-[Ddolddol] Someone dropped it.

1402
01:07:08,524 --> 01:07:09,817
[♪ contemplative music playing]

1403
01:07:09,901 --> 01:07:11,236
10 MINUTES AGO

1404
01:07:11,319 --> 01:07:12,862
[Pani Bottle] I was on my way
back to our base.

1405
01:07:12,946 --> 01:07:14,614
I was going down the left path.

1406
01:07:18,868 --> 01:07:20,703
I found a notebook on the ground.

1407
01:07:20,787 --> 01:07:24,457
I opened it and saw things scribbled down,
but I couldn't make out the words.

1408
01:07:24,540 --> 01:07:26,709
It could be something,
so I took it just in case.

1409
01:07:28,419 --> 01:07:32,131
It's a completely ridiculous gamble,
but this lost notebook could be legit.

1410
01:07:32,215 --> 01:07:33,216
No, that can't be.

1411
01:07:33,299 --> 01:07:34,676
-For real?
-[Pani Bottle] It could be fake.

1412
01:07:34,759 --> 01:07:36,678
But it says, "Horseking, 1, 9."

1413
01:07:36,761 --> 01:07:39,389
It looks like Joonsu's.
It says, "I want to go home."

1414
01:07:39,472 --> 01:07:40,598
[Pani Bottle] "Just fucking" what?

1415
01:07:40,682 --> 01:07:42,642
-"Seven boxes. Fuck"?
-[Jimin] It's Joonsu's notebook.

1416
01:07:42,725 --> 01:07:43,726
NOTEBOOK SEEMS TO BE JOONSU'S

1417
01:07:44,394 --> 01:07:46,104
[Ddolddol] I don't think
we can believe this.

1418
01:07:46,187 --> 01:07:47,939
Should we keep it as a reference?

1419
01:07:48,064 --> 01:07:49,357
[Jimin] Yeah, just as a reference.

1420
01:07:49,440 --> 01:07:51,484
[Ddolddol] It was clearly
Joonsu's notebook.

1421
01:07:52,151 --> 01:07:56,030
But it had the opposing team's ranks
listed inside.

1422
01:07:56,114 --> 01:07:59,534
It looked like
they had written down their ranks

1423
01:07:59,617 --> 01:08:01,869
in the notebook during their meeting.

1424
01:08:01,953 --> 01:08:03,955
It said Horseking had a 9 and 1

1425
01:08:04,038 --> 01:08:06,374
and Jaegyun was the King.

1426
01:08:08,334 --> 01:08:10,878
This seems pretty convincing. But hold on.

1427
01:08:11,462 --> 01:08:12,755
Let me see.

1428
01:08:12,839 --> 01:08:14,090
[Jimin] Jaegyun is the King?

1429
01:08:14,799 --> 01:08:16,092
HORSEKING: 9, 1
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1430
01:08:16,175 --> 01:08:18,553
They really made this look convincing.

1431
01:08:18,636 --> 01:08:20,638
-They made it like what we would've done
-[Jimin] Yeah.

1432
01:08:20,722 --> 01:08:21,806
to make it annoying as well.

1433
01:08:22,348 --> 01:08:23,766
It does look convincing.

1434
01:08:23,850 --> 01:08:26,227
It's so convincing,
and things are going as written.

1435
01:08:26,769 --> 01:08:31,816
[Jimin] I believed the notebook was legit
because I saw Joonsu looking for something

1436
01:08:31,899 --> 01:08:33,609
after the first round.

1437
01:08:37,488 --> 01:08:40,825
Plus, Horseking didn't hesitate
to tag early on.

1438
01:08:40,908 --> 01:08:42,452
[gasps] I thought, "What's this?"

1439
01:08:42,535 --> 01:08:46,205
The King wouldn't be acting
that aggressively at the start.

1440
01:08:46,289 --> 01:08:47,498
I think this is legit.

1441
01:08:47,582 --> 01:08:48,624
Yeah.

1442
01:08:48,708 --> 01:08:51,044
They decided to have the 9 get involved.

1443
01:08:51,127 --> 01:08:53,671
Then, is this real... Hell, this is hard.

1444
01:08:54,380 --> 01:08:57,342
HORSEKING: 9, 1
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1445
01:09:01,763 --> 01:09:03,306
Then, I'll check Horseking.

1446
01:09:04,474 --> 01:09:07,810
Isn't it too risky?
Horseking could be either the 9 or King.

1447
01:09:07,894 --> 01:09:09,270
Still, if I verify him,

1448
01:09:09,354 --> 01:09:10,355
we can either rule out

1449
01:09:10,438 --> 01:09:11,647
-or be sure he's the King.
-[Jimin] Right,

1450
01:09:11,731 --> 01:09:12,732
That's true.

1451
01:09:12,815 --> 01:09:14,359
Junseo should tag Horseking this time.

1452
01:09:14,442 --> 01:09:15,443
RED TEAM'S TARGET: HORSEKING

1453
01:09:15,526 --> 01:09:16,611
[Horseking] What the heck?

1454
01:09:16,694 --> 01:09:17,695
MEANWHILE, BLUE TEAM

1455
01:09:17,779 --> 01:09:19,238
[Horseking] Their strategy seems strange.

1456
01:09:19,322 --> 01:09:20,323
[Jaegyun] What about it?

1457
01:09:20,406 --> 01:09:22,033
Why would they just charge in?

1458
01:09:22,658 --> 01:09:25,161
I wondered,
"How many moves ahead did they plan?"

1459
01:09:25,244 --> 01:09:27,789
"Isn't this too elaborate?"

1460
01:09:27,872 --> 01:09:29,165
I'm wondering what their plan was.

1461
01:09:29,248 --> 01:09:30,750
-They all came at once.
-They came together.

1462
01:09:30,833 --> 01:09:31,959
We didn't even stop them.

1463
01:09:32,043 --> 01:09:34,337
It doesn't make sense
for them to come at us like that.

1464
01:09:34,420 --> 01:09:35,880
It makes no sense. I was startled.

1465
01:09:35,963 --> 01:09:38,049
I remember thinking,
"What's gotten into them?"

1466
01:09:38,132 --> 01:09:39,133
BOTH TEAMS ARE CONFUSED

1467
01:09:39,217 --> 01:09:41,135
They all came, so I was confused.

1468
01:09:41,219 --> 01:09:42,970
Eunsil got tagged by me, right?

1469
01:09:43,054 --> 01:09:44,305
Let's get rid of her.

1470
01:09:44,389 --> 01:09:45,390
Once you run into Eunsil,

1471
01:09:45,473 --> 01:09:46,474
-just tag her.
-I will.

1472
01:09:46,557 --> 01:09:47,558
Yes, that's my plan.

1473
01:09:47,642 --> 01:09:49,644
Once one of them gets eliminated...

1474
01:09:49,727 --> 01:09:52,146
-[ZZONE] They'll fall like dominoes.
-...it'll put us way ahead.

1475
01:09:52,230 --> 01:09:54,774
[Jaegyun] You go after Eunsil.
She doesn't have the King.

1476
01:09:54,857 --> 01:09:55,900
BLUE TEAM'S TARGET: EUNSIL

1477
01:09:55,983 --> 01:09:57,735
Are we starting now?
Will we hear the alarm?

1478
01:09:57,819 --> 01:10:00,071
AFTER 5-MINUTE TEAM MEETING,
SIREN SIGNALS NEW ROUND

1479
01:10:00,154 --> 01:10:01,823
-I hate that alarm.
-Let's go.

1480
01:10:03,032 --> 01:10:04,784
[alarm blaring]

1481
01:10:04,867 --> 01:10:05,910
I'll tag Horseking.

1482
01:10:07,787 --> 01:10:08,913
[Horseking] Let's look around for now.

1483
01:10:09,455 --> 01:10:11,541
[host] The Battle Round has begun.

1484
01:10:11,624 --> 01:10:13,793
[Horseking] Search around.
We'll keep watch here.

1485
01:10:15,420 --> 01:10:17,755
-They're walking toward us!
-They're coming!

1486
01:10:17,839 --> 01:10:19,757
-Horseking sees us.
-Let's go to the Neutral Zone.

1487
01:10:19,841 --> 01:10:20,842
Okay.

1488
01:10:21,592 --> 01:10:23,177
There are four on this side!

1489
01:10:23,761 --> 01:10:25,638
-[ZZONE] I don't see Eunsil.
-[Horseking] Four here!

1490
01:10:29,851 --> 01:10:30,893
Eunsil's not there?

1491
01:10:30,977 --> 01:10:32,478
-No, she's hiding.
-I don't see her.

1492
01:10:32,562 --> 01:10:34,021
BLUE TEAM'S PLAN HITS A SNAG

1493
01:10:34,105 --> 01:10:35,606
RED TEAM BASE, 2ND FLOOR

1494
01:10:36,899 --> 01:10:40,903
[Eunsil] I lost one card,
so I couldn't afford to take any risks.

1495
01:10:42,113 --> 01:10:44,907
We decided I should hide
and wait for our chance.

1496
01:10:45,992 --> 01:10:48,244
So, I hid somewhere out of sight.

1497
01:10:48,327 --> 01:10:51,122
[Ddolddol] How about we act like
we're not tagging Horseking

1498
01:10:51,205 --> 01:10:52,457
then suddenly go for him?

1499
01:10:52,540 --> 01:10:54,292
[Junseo] Pretend we're searching.
This way.

1500
01:10:54,375 --> 01:10:55,376
[Ddolddol] This way?

1501
01:10:55,460 --> 01:10:57,295
-Should we check the furniture?
-[Junseo] Yes.

1502
01:10:58,254 --> 01:10:59,255
THEY PLAN TO BAIT HORSEKING

1503
01:10:59,338 --> 01:11:00,465
-[Ddolddol] Shall we go in here?
-[Junseo] Yes.

1504
01:11:00,548 --> 01:11:01,549
[Ddolddol] Let's get inside.

1505
01:11:02,091 --> 01:11:05,094
[Horseking] They're searching over there.
We'll search here.

1506
01:11:05,178 --> 01:11:06,220
-[Jaegyun] We should too.
-[ZZONE] Let's hurry

1507
01:11:06,304 --> 01:11:07,430
-and find them.
-[Jaegyun] Let's search.

1508
01:11:07,513 --> 01:11:08,890
Dail, let's search.

1509
01:11:08,973 --> 01:11:11,225
BLUE TEAM SEARCHES FOR SYMBOLS
AS A BACKUP PLAN

1510
01:11:11,809 --> 01:11:12,935
[Horseking] We don't have any yet!

1511
01:11:21,319 --> 01:11:22,904
Searching the reeds is no joke.

1512
01:11:23,863 --> 01:11:28,951
AND RED TEAM IS WATCHING

1513
01:11:29,035 --> 01:11:31,120
[♪ tense music playing]

1514
01:11:31,204 --> 01:11:32,872
[Horseking] Junseo's coming.
Junseo's coming.

1515
01:11:34,582 --> 01:11:35,833
[Jimin] We need to get Horseking.

1516
01:11:38,377 --> 01:11:39,921
RED TEAM CLOSES IN ON HORSEKING

1517
01:11:40,004 --> 01:11:41,047
[Ddolddol] Wait a moment.

1518
01:11:41,631 --> 01:11:42,799
[Horseking] I'm not going to do it.

1519
01:11:44,342 --> 01:11:47,303
[Junseo] Since I had to find out
what card Horseking had,

1520
01:11:48,429 --> 01:11:49,889
I was waiting for the right moment.

1521
01:11:50,640 --> 01:11:52,266
Wait, I need someone to watch my back.

1522
01:11:53,893 --> 01:11:57,188
Jaegyun! Hey, Dail!
I need you to cover me.

1523
01:11:57,814 --> 01:12:00,107
You have to get my back, Jaegyun!

1524
01:12:03,611 --> 01:12:04,737
BLUE TEAM FOUND A SYMBOL

1525
01:12:04,821 --> 01:12:06,155
[♪ rock music playing]

1526
01:12:08,783 --> 01:12:09,909
[Jaegyun] I found it.

1527
01:12:11,077 --> 01:12:12,662
[♪ music continues playing]

1528
01:12:12,745 --> 01:12:15,456
A SYMBOL HIDDEN IN THE REEDS

1529
01:12:18,709 --> 01:12:20,294
[Horseking] Let's pull back. Pull back.

1530
01:12:21,879 --> 01:12:22,880
[Jimin] Fuck.

1531
01:12:25,466 --> 01:12:26,843
[Dail] Junseo is running!

1532
01:12:27,885 --> 01:12:29,011
Junseo's behind you!

1533
01:12:34,308 --> 01:12:35,685
-[Jimin] Watch out!
-[Ddolddol] Be careful

1534
01:12:39,313 --> 01:12:41,399
DISTANCE CREATED INSTANTLY

1535
01:12:41,482 --> 01:12:46,529
[Jaegyun] I handed Horseking the symbol
while he was being chased by Junseo.

1536
01:12:47,446 --> 01:12:48,865
SYMBOL HANDED TO HORSEKING

1537
01:12:53,494 --> 01:12:54,495
BLUE TEAM DESTROYS ONE SYMBOL

1538
01:12:57,540 --> 01:12:59,000
It's impossible to catch Horseking.

1539
01:12:59,083 --> 01:13:00,251
SYMBOL DESTRUCTION STATUS

1540
01:13:00,793 --> 01:13:04,088
FAILED TO TAKE DOWN HORSEKING

1541
01:13:04,171 --> 01:13:06,674
MEANWHILE

1542
01:13:06,757 --> 01:13:10,261
JOONSU IS LOOKING FOR SOMETHING

1543
01:13:10,887 --> 01:13:11,888
[frustrated groan]

1544
01:13:13,681 --> 01:13:14,891
[Pani Bottle] Who is it?

1545
01:13:16,642 --> 01:13:18,352
Joonsu was coming toward me.

1546
01:13:18,436 --> 01:13:19,687
He kept looking around.

1547
01:13:19,770 --> 01:13:22,565
And that was the exact spot
where the notebook was found.

1548
01:13:24,859 --> 01:13:25,860
Well, look at this.

1549
01:13:27,153 --> 01:13:29,196
Should we go our separate ways? [laughs]

1550
01:13:30,239 --> 01:13:31,866
Joonsu! Get him.

1551
01:13:33,242 --> 01:13:34,243
[Joonsu sighs]

1552
01:13:37,663 --> 01:13:39,165
JOONSU TAGS PANI BOTTLE

1553
01:13:39,248 --> 01:13:40,291
-[alarm blaring]
-[Joonsu] I got him!

1554
01:13:40,917 --> 01:13:42,335
[host] Tag confirmed.

1555
01:13:42,877 --> 01:13:44,879
I found it strange that he tagged me.

1556
01:13:44,962 --> 01:13:46,547
Why would he tag me?

1557
01:13:47,548 --> 01:13:50,009
Since I considered him a weaker player,

1558
01:13:50,593 --> 01:13:52,595
-I was even more confused.
-[♪ mysterious music playing]

1559
01:13:52,678 --> 01:13:56,682
I don't think they would've given
Joonsu an important card.

1560
01:14:04,148 --> 01:14:05,274
[Joonsu] Did you make a choice?

1561
01:14:05,358 --> 01:14:06,442
I'm thinking.

1562
01:14:07,526 --> 01:14:09,403
[Joonsu] I'll go first then.

1563
01:14:11,197 --> 01:14:12,406
This is mine. Joonsu's card.

1564
01:14:12,490 --> 01:14:13,824
LEE JOONSU HANDS IN A CARD

1565
01:14:16,077 --> 01:14:17,954
[sighs wearily]

1566
01:14:18,037 --> 01:14:19,372
[Pani Bottle] I was sure
he wasn't the King,

1567
01:14:19,455 --> 01:14:21,248
and the Joker was even less likely.

1568
01:14:22,208 --> 01:14:27,046
So I used a 2 to test the waters.

1569
01:14:28,839 --> 01:14:30,508
[dealer] We will announce the results.

1570
01:14:33,344 --> 01:14:35,805
Lee Joonsu has won.

1571
01:14:38,307 --> 01:14:39,308
[Pani Bottle] I'm good to go, right?

1572
01:14:39,392 --> 01:14:42,812
PANI BOTTLE'S 2 GOES TO JOONSU

1573
01:14:44,981 --> 01:14:46,315
Joonsu won.

1574
01:14:46,399 --> 01:14:48,985
[Junseo] It's fine.
Only two cards are out.

1575
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:52,279
[Jimin] And what Joonsu took was a 2.

1576
01:14:52,947 --> 01:14:55,032
He played either a 4 or 7.

1577
01:14:55,116 --> 01:14:57,326
If he'd played a 7,
then he only has a 4 and 2.

1578
01:14:57,451 --> 01:14:59,161
It means he's weak as fuck.

1579
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:01,998
[Dail] Joonsu has a different number now.

1580
01:15:02,081 --> 01:15:03,082
-[ZZONE] Right.
-[Jaegyun] Yes, he does.

1581
01:15:04,000 --> 01:15:05,918
Joonsu's got a 2 and 4.

1582
01:15:06,544 --> 01:15:08,337
Yes, if they go after him
to beat his 2 or 4,

1583
01:15:08,421 --> 01:15:10,631
one of us has to come help him.

1584
01:15:10,715 --> 01:15:12,341
Then, I'll avoid them.

1585
01:15:12,425 --> 01:15:13,968
-Yeah, avoid them.
-Avoid them.

1586
01:15:14,051 --> 01:15:16,387
I think the notebook is correct.

1587
01:15:17,221 --> 01:15:19,974
Horseking kept telling Jaegyun,
"Jaegyun! I need you to cover me."

1588
01:15:20,057 --> 01:15:22,643
"I need you to protect me."
He was saying things like that.

1589
01:15:23,185 --> 01:15:25,187
Wait, I need someone to watch my back.

1590
01:15:25,271 --> 01:15:27,690
Jaegyun! Hey, Dail!
I need you to cover me.

1591
01:15:27,773 --> 01:15:28,858
HORSEKING ASKED JAEGYUN FOR HELP

1592
01:15:28,941 --> 01:15:31,235
I think Horseking was afraid
of getting tagged by the King.

1593
01:15:31,318 --> 01:15:32,319
[Jimin] Right.

1594
01:15:32,403 --> 01:15:35,031
[Ddolddol] Then,
only the King could protect him.

1595
01:15:35,114 --> 01:15:37,241
Would he ask the Joker to protect him? No.

1596
01:15:37,783 --> 01:15:40,077
If we identify who King is,
that's all we need.

1597
01:15:40,161 --> 01:15:42,955
Tagging Horseking and Jaegyun
should reveal the answer.

1598
01:15:43,039 --> 01:15:44,165
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1599
01:15:44,248 --> 01:15:46,917
The four of us should go together...

1600
01:15:47,001 --> 01:15:48,461
-Let's move together.
-...one after another.

1601
01:15:48,544 --> 01:15:50,254
-Let's go as a group.
-[Ddolddol] Attack in waves.

1602
01:15:50,337 --> 01:15:52,256
Let's go all together and tag someone.

1603
01:15:52,339 --> 01:15:53,466
RED TEAM WILL MOVE AS ONE AGAIN

1604
01:15:53,549 --> 01:15:55,468
-[Pani Bottle] They're hiding too.
-I'll go along.

1605
01:15:55,551 --> 01:15:58,387
Four of us will stick together,
and I'll try to tag them.

1606
01:15:58,471 --> 01:16:00,306
If we fail, just tag anyone.

1607
01:16:00,389 --> 01:16:01,640
-Me?
-Yeah, if it falls through.

1608
01:16:04,727 --> 01:16:06,812
[Pani Bottle] Should I put down
an 8 to check?

1609
01:16:06,896 --> 01:16:07,938
Use the 8 on Jaegyun.

1610
01:16:08,022 --> 01:16:10,107
[host] The Battle Round has begun.

1611
01:16:13,652 --> 01:16:14,653
[Joonsu] Four over here!

1612
01:16:14,737 --> 01:16:15,905
SPOTS RED TEAM ON OTHER SIDE

1613
01:16:16,447 --> 01:16:17,448
Is Pani Bottle here?

1614
01:16:17,531 --> 01:16:18,574
Get ready to tag!

1615
01:16:20,034 --> 01:16:21,368
Pani Bottle is coming!

1616
01:16:23,329 --> 01:16:24,830
Jaegyun's over there.

1617
01:16:24,914 --> 01:16:25,998
-[Ddolddol] Where?
-[Junseo] On the right.

1618
01:16:26,540 --> 01:16:28,459
-Horseking is in the middle.
-[Ddolddol] Okay.

1619
01:16:30,086 --> 01:16:31,128
[ZZONE] This is so scary.

1620
01:16:35,174 --> 01:16:37,218
-[Ddolddol] Who should go first?
-[Junseo] I'll go first.

1621
01:16:37,301 --> 01:16:39,053
-If I fail, just tag anyone.
-[Ddolddol] Okay.

1622
01:16:39,178 --> 01:16:40,721
-[Junseo] You can tag either of them.
-[Ddolddol] Okay.

1623
01:16:41,138 --> 01:16:42,723
RED TEAM'S TARGET: JAEGYUN, HORSEKING

1624
01:16:42,807 --> 01:16:45,434
[Junseo] First, we moved
as a group of four as we planned.

1625
01:16:46,685 --> 01:16:48,521
[Horseking] Be careful!
ZZONE, move out of the way.

1626
01:16:50,356 --> 01:16:51,690
Pani Bottle is running!

1627
01:16:52,191 --> 01:16:54,443
[Junseo] Once things get chaotic,
get behind them and strike.

1628
01:16:55,945 --> 01:16:58,239
RED TEAM MAKES THEIR MOVE

1629
01:16:59,907 --> 01:17:01,075
[Horseking] Junseo's coming for me.

1630
01:17:02,743 --> 01:17:06,789
[Junseo] I was targeting
Horseking and Jaegyun.

1631
01:17:08,207 --> 01:17:10,668
-Then, Jaegyun protected him from me.
-[Jaegyun exclaims]

1632
01:17:13,045 --> 01:17:15,256
YUK JUNSEO TAGS HWANG JAEGYUN

1633
01:17:15,339 --> 01:17:16,507
[alarm blaring]

1634
01:17:16,590 --> 01:17:17,967
[host] Tag confirmed.

1635
01:17:18,050 --> 01:17:19,468
-[Horseking] Junseo should be the King.
-[Jaegyun] What?

1636
01:17:19,552 --> 01:17:20,553
[Horseking] Junseo is the King.

1637
01:17:21,345 --> 01:17:22,555
Is this right?

1638
01:17:23,556 --> 01:17:27,768
[sighs] I think you should've ran
straight for Pani Bottle.

1639
01:17:28,769 --> 01:17:30,271
-That notebook's 100% legit.
-[Ddolddol] Yes.

1640
01:17:30,354 --> 01:17:32,356
[Pani Bottle] Horseking didn't tag me.

1641
01:17:32,439 --> 01:17:33,774
[Ddolddol] He could have,
but he didn't chase me.

1642
01:17:33,858 --> 01:17:34,900
Because it's a waste.

1643
01:17:34,984 --> 01:17:35,985
DESPERATELY AVOIDING JUNSEO

1644
01:17:36,068 --> 01:17:37,403
[Jimin] And since you have a 2,

1645
01:17:37,486 --> 01:17:39,572
he definitely assumes
your other card is high.

1646
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:41,407
[Pani Bottle] I kept
thinking it over like hell.

1647
01:17:42,283 --> 01:17:43,617
[Jimin] You did amazing.

1648
01:17:43,701 --> 01:17:45,703
So the notebook was legit.

1649
01:17:46,453 --> 01:17:49,540
Horseking became more passive
and didn't tag Pani Bottle.

1650
01:17:50,124 --> 01:17:52,543
Jaegyun actively protected Horseking.

1651
01:17:53,586 --> 01:17:55,629
Jaegyun has to be the King.

1652
01:17:55,713 --> 01:17:57,173
CONVINCED JAEGYUN IS KING

1653
01:17:58,340 --> 01:18:01,385
By the way,
Jaegyun's got either a King or 6.

1654
01:18:01,969 --> 01:18:04,597
-Could he pull out a 6?
-Beats me.

1655
01:18:04,680 --> 01:18:06,932
He could played a 6.
If he believed Junseo was the King,

1656
01:18:07,016 --> 01:18:08,475
he can't play his King.

1657
01:18:08,559 --> 01:18:10,102
Then, he gets exposed as the King.

1658
01:18:11,645 --> 01:18:13,147
Then, he might play the 6.

1659
01:18:13,772 --> 01:18:15,566
-But if he does, thank you.
-[Ddolddol] Thank you so much.

1660
01:18:15,649 --> 01:18:17,985
We just need to catch
and eliminate Hwang Jaegyun.

1661
01:18:20,154 --> 01:18:21,739
[dealer] We will announce the results.

1662
01:18:21,822 --> 01:18:23,157
HWANG JAEGYUN VS. YUK JUNSEO

1663
01:18:24,575 --> 01:18:26,869
Yuk Junseo has won.

1664
01:18:27,703 --> 01:18:30,372
Mr. Yuk Junseo,
please come and take the card.

1665
01:18:32,708 --> 01:18:34,752
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1666
01:18:38,839 --> 01:18:39,840
[sighs]

1667
01:18:41,091 --> 01:18:42,468
[Ddolddol] I wonder how it turned out.

1668
01:18:46,555 --> 01:18:47,556
What did you play?

1669
01:18:49,516 --> 01:18:50,726
I played an 8.

1670
01:18:50,809 --> 01:18:52,394
-[Pani Bottle] An 8?
-Jaegyun played a 7.

1671
01:18:53,771 --> 01:18:54,772
What?

1672
01:18:55,981 --> 01:18:57,107
-Jaegyun played...
-[Pani Bottle] An 8 and 7?

1673
01:18:57,316 --> 01:18:58,525
-...a 7?
-[Junseo] Yes.

1674
01:18:59,610 --> 01:19:00,945
So the notebook was wrong.

1675
01:19:01,028 --> 01:19:03,656
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1676
01:19:03,739 --> 01:19:05,449
[Ddolddol] Wait,
we need an emergency meeting.

1677
01:19:06,116 --> 01:19:07,576
My mind seriously went blank. [chuckles]

1678
01:19:08,869 --> 01:19:13,040
Junseo played an 8
and claimed Jaegyun's 7.

1679
01:19:13,123 --> 01:19:17,294
The notebook said Jaegyun had
a King and 6, but he played a 7?

1680
01:19:17,378 --> 01:19:18,379
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1681
01:19:18,462 --> 01:19:23,884
RED TEAM IN CONFUSION

1682
01:19:27,096 --> 01:19:28,180
So, this is wrong?

1683
01:19:30,057 --> 01:19:33,227
But I don't think it's a lot different
from this, don't you think?

1684
01:19:33,310 --> 01:19:35,187
I do think Jaegyun is the King.

1685
01:19:35,271 --> 01:19:37,773
But think about it.
If I were the King and had a 7,

1686
01:19:37,856 --> 01:19:39,358
would I play the 7 first?

1687
01:19:39,441 --> 01:19:40,901
I'd be completely vulnerable.

1688
01:19:40,985 --> 01:19:43,153
I'd just play a regular card.

1689
01:19:43,237 --> 01:19:45,572
Especially with everyone suspecting
Junseo as the King,

1690
01:19:45,656 --> 01:19:47,825
if I put down the King
and nothing happens,

1691
01:19:47,908 --> 01:19:49,159
then the game's over.

1692
01:19:49,243 --> 01:19:50,244
JIMIN THINKS IT'LL BE SIMILAR

1693
01:19:50,327 --> 01:19:52,288
But this might be fake.

1694
01:19:52,371 --> 01:19:55,082
I'm afraid we're relying too much on this.

1695
01:19:55,165 --> 01:19:56,709
Should I check Horseking?

1696
01:19:57,418 --> 01:19:59,670
Horseking does keep running away.

1697
01:19:59,753 --> 01:20:02,339
Ddolddol can step up...

1698
01:20:02,423 --> 01:20:05,217
Who do I need to avoid going up against?

1699
01:20:05,301 --> 01:20:07,136
-Just not against Jaegyun.
-[Ddolddol] Right?

1700
01:20:07,636 --> 01:20:08,846
[Junseo] Ddolddol,
want to eliminate Horseking?

1701
01:20:08,929 --> 01:20:09,930
Okay.

1702
01:20:10,014 --> 01:20:11,390
DDOLDDOL WILL ELIMINATE HORSEKING

1703
01:20:11,974 --> 01:20:13,559
[ZZONE] We've found
only one symbol, right?

1704
01:20:13,642 --> 01:20:15,227
-[Jaegyun] Yes.
-[ZZONE sighs]

1705
01:20:15,311 --> 01:20:16,353
I can't find any.

1706
01:20:16,437 --> 01:20:18,772
[ZZONE] Right?
We can't find anything in the reeds.

1707
01:20:18,856 --> 01:20:20,316
[Dail] We need to find symbols.

1708
01:20:20,399 --> 01:20:22,192
We need to keep going to the Reed Field.

1709
01:20:22,276 --> 01:20:24,695
Once it's dark,
we can't find any in the reeds.

1710
01:20:26,030 --> 01:20:27,990
If you can avoid getting caught
until I make my move,

1711
01:20:28,073 --> 01:20:29,992
I'll try to get one.

1712
01:20:30,075 --> 01:20:31,618
Let's try to find four first.

1713
01:20:31,702 --> 01:20:32,995
BLUE TEAM'S GOAL: FIND SYMBOLS

1714
01:20:33,537 --> 01:20:36,040
-[host] The Battle Round has begun.
-[alarm blaring]

1715
01:20:36,123 --> 01:20:37,374
[Ddolddol] That one?

1716
01:20:37,458 --> 01:20:38,459
[Jimin] Let's go!

1717
01:20:38,542 --> 01:20:39,626
[Pani Bottle] This way.

1718
01:20:39,710 --> 01:20:40,711
-[Pani Bottle] To the left.
-[Ddolddol] Left?

1719
01:20:40,794 --> 01:20:42,338
-[Pani Bottle] Yes, left.
-[Ddolddol] Okay, let's go to the left.

1720
01:20:43,714 --> 01:20:44,715
They're all coming!

1721
01:20:45,507 --> 01:20:46,759
They're all here!

1722
01:20:46,842 --> 01:20:49,178
EXCEPT FOR EUNSIL,
RED TEAM HEADS TO THE OTHER BASE

1723
01:20:49,261 --> 01:20:51,055
[Horseking] I'll go around.
Keep an eye on it.

1724
01:20:51,764 --> 01:20:55,142
Those four came back without Eunsil,
as if they were out taking a stroll.

1725
01:20:56,185 --> 01:20:59,271
I just need to find a symbol,
so let's focus on that.

1726
01:21:00,939 --> 01:21:03,650
[♪ exciting music playing]

1727
01:21:03,734 --> 01:21:04,777
[Joonsu] Where could it be?

1728
01:21:07,529 --> 01:21:09,239
[ZZONE] It's so hard to find them.

1729
01:21:11,492 --> 01:21:12,493
[Jimin] Where are they?

1730
01:21:12,576 --> 01:21:13,911
[Pani Bottle] They're searching
over there.

1731
01:21:14,828 --> 01:21:16,538
Right. I saw ZZONE.

1732
01:21:16,622 --> 01:21:18,832
[Jimin] Why are they searching so hard?

1733
01:21:18,916 --> 01:21:22,378
He checks that over and over again.
Nothing was there earlier, so why?

1734
01:21:22,461 --> 01:21:24,880
-[Ddolddol] Should we follow Dail?
-[Jimin] Dail's running like crazy.

1735
01:21:25,964 --> 01:21:27,383
I need to catch Horseking.

1736
01:21:29,676 --> 01:21:35,891
RED TEAM BASE

1737
01:21:37,476 --> 01:21:39,728
[Horseking] There was no one
in the opposing team's base.

1738
01:21:42,314 --> 01:21:43,315
[Junseo] Let's go search
since no one's here.

1739
01:21:43,399 --> 01:21:44,400
[Ddolddol] Okay.

1740
01:21:44,483 --> 01:21:46,068
ENTIRE RED TEAM EXCEPT EUNSIL
IS OUTSIDE

1741
01:21:46,151 --> 01:21:47,861
[panting]

1742
01:21:50,072 --> 01:21:51,698
[Horseking] I looked
around the second floor...

1743
01:21:55,285 --> 01:21:56,662
and found it right away.

1744
01:21:56,745 --> 01:21:58,747
[♪ exciting music playing]

1745
01:22:08,173 --> 01:22:09,258
[Jimin] Horseking!

1746
01:22:10,008 --> 01:22:12,511
SPOTS HORSEKING
WHO HAS FOUND A SYMBOL

1747
01:22:12,594 --> 01:22:13,595
[Ddolddol] Horseking is here!

1748
01:22:13,679 --> 01:22:16,265
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1749
01:22:16,348 --> 01:22:19,059
There he was.
Horseking was right in front of me.

1750
01:22:19,560 --> 01:22:21,437
[Junseo] Catch them!

1751
01:22:24,857 --> 01:22:26,066
FAILS TO TAG

1752
01:22:26,525 --> 01:22:28,569
[Horseking] In that moment, I knew
I couldn't let myself get caught.

1753
01:22:28,652 --> 01:22:31,321
I thought,
"Run like your life depends on it."

1754
01:22:33,073 --> 01:22:36,034
JUNSEO HEADS THE OTHER WAY

1755
01:22:36,452 --> 01:22:38,078
HORSEKING ENTERS THE BASE

1756
01:22:38,162 --> 01:22:39,329
PANI BOTTLE SHOWS UP

1757
01:22:47,504 --> 01:22:48,630
[Pani Bottle] I dropped it.

1758
01:22:48,714 --> 01:22:49,715
FAILS TO TAG

1759
01:22:49,798 --> 01:22:51,175
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1760
01:23:00,642 --> 01:23:01,643
[Horseking] It's over.

1761
01:23:01,727 --> 01:23:03,479
-I'm here.
-[Junseo] You didn't break it yet.

1762
01:23:03,562 --> 01:23:05,314
No, I have to give this to them to check.

1763
01:23:05,772 --> 01:23:07,733
[host] Tagging isn't allowed
in the Dealer Room.

1764
01:23:07,816 --> 01:23:08,817
[Horseking] You can't in here.

1765
01:23:08,901 --> 01:23:11,028
THE TARGET NARROWLY ESCAPED

1766
01:23:15,991 --> 01:23:18,660
BLUE TEAM DESTROYS SECOND SYMBOL

1767
01:23:18,744 --> 01:23:20,704
[panting]

1768
01:23:22,456 --> 01:23:23,457
[Junseo] I couldn't get him.

1769
01:23:23,540 --> 01:23:24,791
-[Ddolddol] What?
-[Junseo] I couldn't get him.

1770
01:23:25,709 --> 01:23:28,545
He was seriously fast. Why is he so fast?

1771
01:23:28,629 --> 01:23:30,172
I thought he was a cheetah.

1772
01:23:30,255 --> 01:23:32,466
[Horseking panting heavily]

1773
01:23:36,803 --> 01:23:37,804
[Horseking] What on earth?

1774
01:23:38,764 --> 01:23:40,974
[Ddolddol] Did you break it? [groans]

1775
01:23:46,271 --> 01:23:49,816
THE KING IS CONSIDERING TAGGING

1776
01:23:52,319 --> 01:23:54,530
HORSEKING TURNS AND COMES BACK

1777
01:23:57,908 --> 01:23:59,576
KIM DDOLDDOL TAGS HORSEKING

1778
01:23:59,660 --> 01:24:00,702
Let's go.

1779
01:24:00,786 --> 01:24:02,538
[host] Tag confirmed.

1780
01:24:03,497 --> 01:24:05,499
I really wanted to check Horseking.

1781
01:24:05,582 --> 01:24:08,252
It was obvious he had a high card.

1782
01:24:09,086 --> 01:24:12,297
If I was the King
and went up against a high card,

1783
01:24:12,381 --> 01:24:14,716
there was a risk of getting exposed.

1784
01:24:15,259 --> 01:24:17,803
But I wanted to use this chance

1785
01:24:17,886 --> 01:24:20,639
to figure out Horseking's rank.

1786
01:24:23,016 --> 01:24:24,017
This is Horseking.

1787
01:24:37,906 --> 01:24:41,201
KIM DDOLDDOL SUBMITS THE KING CARD

1788
01:24:45,789 --> 01:24:47,207
[dealer] We will announce the results.

1789
01:24:49,626 --> 01:24:51,420
[Pani Bottle] I think
we have the advantage now.

1790
01:24:51,503 --> 01:24:54,548
We have a huge advantage.
And we took out a strong card.

1791
01:24:54,631 --> 01:24:56,300
-[Pani Bottle] Yes, the 7 is gone.
-That's crazy good.

1792
01:24:57,050 --> 01:24:58,719
[ZZONE] They got that annoying Ddolddol.

1793
01:24:58,802 --> 01:25:01,763
[Jaegyun] But we don't know
what Ddolddol has.

1794
01:25:01,847 --> 01:25:03,056
[ZZONE exhales sharply]

1795
01:25:04,850 --> 01:25:05,934
[Horseking exhales sharply]

1796
01:25:06,018 --> 01:25:07,019
[Joonsu] Who won?

1797
01:25:07,102 --> 01:25:08,395
[Horseking] What?

1798
01:25:09,104 --> 01:25:11,607
[exhales] I can't run anymore.

1799
01:25:16,028 --> 01:25:17,195
[Ddolddol] This is an emergency.

1800
01:25:19,615 --> 01:25:21,325
[dealer] We will check both of your cards.

1801
01:25:21,408 --> 01:25:25,078
KIM DDOLDDOL: KING

1802
01:25:25,162 --> 01:25:27,205
HORSEKING: KING

1803
01:25:29,625 --> 01:25:31,168
[dealer] We will announce the results.

1804
01:25:31,960 --> 01:25:32,961
It's a tie.

1805
01:25:33,629 --> 01:25:35,130
Please take your cards.

1806
01:25:35,213 --> 01:25:36,423
KIM DDOLDDOL AND HORSEKING TIE

1807
01:25:38,175 --> 01:25:42,387
At that point, I thought, "I'm screwed."

1808
01:25:43,889 --> 01:25:47,059
I went in just to tag someone.

1809
01:25:47,142 --> 01:25:49,686
But of all people,
I ended up tagging the King.

1810
01:25:50,270 --> 01:25:51,605
How did I not see this coming?

1811
01:25:51,688 --> 01:25:55,942
He's Horseking. It's right in his name.
Why did I tag the King? I was so stupid.

1812
01:25:56,026 --> 01:25:57,027
[in English] Horseking.

1813
01:25:57,569 --> 01:25:58,570
[in Korean] K for "King."

1814
01:26:05,911 --> 01:26:08,288
[Ddolddol] Horseking and I
are both Kings. [sighs]

1815
01:26:10,332 --> 01:26:11,583
We were completely off.

1816
01:26:12,250 --> 01:26:13,251
[Pani Bottle] Hmm?

1817
01:26:14,419 --> 01:26:15,462
He's the King?

1818
01:26:15,545 --> 01:26:16,963
[Ddolddol] We both confirmed
we're the Kings.

1819
01:26:17,047 --> 01:26:18,840
-[Jimin] Nothing happened?
-Nope.

1820
01:26:19,716 --> 01:26:22,511
-Can we check out Joonsu's?
-[Ddolddol] Where's his notebook?

1821
01:26:23,345 --> 01:26:24,721
I think he changed it on purpose.

1822
01:26:24,805 --> 01:26:26,264
THE NOTEBOOK SAID JAEGYUN WAS KING

1823
01:26:26,348 --> 01:26:27,432
The King turned out to be him.

1824
01:26:27,516 --> 01:26:28,684
HORSEKING: 9, 1
JAEGYUN: KING, 6

1825
01:26:28,767 --> 01:26:29,893
It's not right, is it?

1826
01:26:29,976 --> 01:26:31,728
[Ddolddol] It's not right.
It's way different, right?

1827
01:26:31,812 --> 01:26:33,772
-It's a lie. It's fake.
-[♪ suspicious music playing]

1828
01:26:33,855 --> 01:26:36,775
Jimin still thought
it could be real until the end.

1829
01:26:36,858 --> 01:26:39,069
But it was just fake.
Things didn't add up.

1830
01:26:39,778 --> 01:26:43,699
Joonsu is capable of coming up
with a strategy like that?

1831
01:26:44,908 --> 01:26:48,578
[Horseking] Jimin clearly
and urgently shouted,

1832
01:26:49,746 --> 01:26:50,831
"Get Horseking!"

1833
01:26:51,373 --> 01:26:52,416
-[Jaegyun] Really?
-[ZZONE] Yes.

1834
01:26:52,499 --> 01:26:54,584
-She's certain it's me.
-[ZZONE] Right. Yeah.

1835
01:26:54,668 --> 01:26:55,711
[Jaegyun] So they took the notebook.

1836
01:26:55,794 --> 01:26:57,254
-[Joonsu] They bought it.
-[Horseking] They took it.

1837
01:26:57,337 --> 01:27:00,340
That was Blue Team's strategy.

1838
01:27:01,174 --> 01:27:02,801
1 HOUR AGO

1839
01:27:02,884 --> 01:27:05,762
[Jaegyun] Don't lose your notebook
after you write down the numbers.

1840
01:27:05,846 --> 01:27:07,180
[both laugh]

1841
01:27:07,264 --> 01:27:08,932
What if we use this against them?

1842
01:27:10,225 --> 01:27:11,226
[Jaegyun] Oh.

1843
01:27:11,309 --> 01:27:12,561
[both laughing]

1844
01:27:13,353 --> 01:27:18,233
We could write, "Horseking is 1 and 9,"
in the notebook and let them find it.

1845
01:27:18,316 --> 01:27:19,317
[Jaegyun] Shall we?

1846
01:27:20,402 --> 01:27:21,653
[whispers] I bet they'd fall for it.

1847
01:27:22,320 --> 01:27:23,739
This should be a lot of fun.

1848
01:27:24,406 --> 01:27:26,158
Make it look legit
with patterns like "1, 9."

1849
01:27:26,241 --> 01:27:27,242
MAKING A FAKE RANK CHART

1850
01:27:27,325 --> 01:27:29,619
Or like "Yang Dail, 2, 8."

1851
01:27:30,287 --> 01:27:32,789
[Joonsu] If they take the bait,
it'll be awesome.

1852
01:27:32,873 --> 01:27:36,543
It probably says Jaegyun was the King,
instead of Horseking.

1853
01:27:37,169 --> 01:27:41,339
In Round 1, all five of them
came along by the reeds.

1854
01:27:41,423 --> 01:27:44,634
That's when I went
into the alley on the right

1855
01:27:44,718 --> 01:27:47,637
and dropped the notebook
where it would look natural.

1856
01:27:48,972 --> 01:27:51,558
When I went back the following round,
it was gone.

1857
01:27:52,309 --> 01:27:53,351
AFTER ROUND 1

1858
01:27:53,435 --> 01:27:54,436
Hey.

1859
01:27:55,437 --> 01:27:56,813
They took my notebook.

1860
01:27:56,897 --> 01:27:57,981
-[Jaegyun] They took it?
-[Joonsu] Yes.

1861
01:27:58,064 --> 01:27:59,691
-Who? Really?
-[Joonsu] Yes, they took it.

1862
01:27:59,775 --> 01:28:00,901
[both laughing]

1863
01:28:00,984 --> 01:28:02,486
-They took it?
-[Joonsu] Yes, they did.

1864
01:28:02,569 --> 01:28:03,653
[ZZONE laughs]

1865
01:28:04,529 --> 01:28:05,614
[Joonsu] This is perfect.

1866
01:28:05,697 --> 01:28:07,407
[groans] I'm so pissed off.

1867
01:28:07,491 --> 01:28:11,244
[sighs] I was tricked by Joonsu?
I didn't want to believe it.

1868
01:28:13,455 --> 01:28:15,373
[Ddolddol] I think we should probably
stop checking this.

1869
01:28:15,457 --> 01:28:16,958
[Pani Bottle] Right, put it away.

1870
01:28:17,042 --> 01:28:19,920
Then, the chances of ZZONE
not being the Joker are really high.

1871
01:28:21,213 --> 01:28:22,881
I don't think ZZONE is the Joker.

1872
01:28:22,964 --> 01:28:24,883
They know we'd obviously think
it was ZZONE.

1873
01:28:25,425 --> 01:28:27,010
[Ddolddol] Then, who received the Joker?

1874
01:28:29,221 --> 01:28:31,473
[Jaegyun] Both teams
have confirmed who the King is.

1875
01:28:31,556 --> 01:28:32,599
[Horseking] Now,
it's about identifying the Joker.

1876
01:28:32,682 --> 01:28:33,683
[Jaegyun] Yes.

1877
01:28:33,767 --> 01:28:36,561
I'm convinced the Joker
is either Junseo or Eunsil.

1878
01:28:36,645 --> 01:28:38,855
I think it's probably one of them.

1879
01:28:38,939 --> 01:28:40,524
Giving the Joker to Junseo...

1880
01:28:41,441 --> 01:28:44,736
I think the Joker is definitely Eunsil,

1881
01:28:44,820 --> 01:28:46,363
-if you ask me.
-Because she's in hiding?

1882
01:28:46,446 --> 01:28:47,447
She's absent.

1883
01:28:47,989 --> 01:28:50,867
EUNSIL HAS BEEN HIDING
THE WHOLE TIME AND IS THE JOKER?

1884
01:28:50,951 --> 01:28:53,119
Yeah, to be honest,
if Eunsil is the Joker,

1885
01:28:53,203 --> 01:28:54,663
-I win.
-[Dail] Yeah.

1886
01:28:54,746 --> 01:28:56,581
No, she has one more.

1887
01:28:56,665 --> 01:28:58,917
-Right, the Joker has three cards.
-[Joonsu] Exactly.

1888
01:28:59,000 --> 01:29:01,086
THE PLAYER WITH THE JOKER CARD
HAS THREE CARDS

1889
01:29:01,670 --> 01:29:04,256
If she had one more card,
why would she play so passively?

1890
01:29:04,339 --> 01:29:05,966
That could be part of their act.

1891
01:29:06,550 --> 01:29:08,635
-The more we think about it...
-[Horseking] I know.

1892
01:29:08,718 --> 01:29:10,762
...we keep thinking about it.

1893
01:29:10,846 --> 01:29:13,223
[Jaegyun] We should
take them out one at a time.

1894
01:29:14,099 --> 01:29:15,100
Let's do that.

1895
01:29:15,183 --> 01:29:16,184
[Jaegyun] Then first,
let's get rid of Eunsil.

1896
01:29:16,268 --> 01:29:17,644
-[Horseking] We have to.
-[alarm blaring]

1897
01:29:17,727 --> 01:29:18,728
Let's go, let's go.

1898
01:29:18,812 --> 01:29:20,188
[♪ thrilling music playing]

1899
01:29:20,772 --> 01:29:22,482
-[ZZONE] Then I'll search.
-[Joonsu] I'll search too.

1900
01:29:23,108 --> 01:29:25,402
[host] The Battle Round has begun.

1901
01:29:28,905 --> 01:29:30,448
How is she hiding so well?

1902
01:29:30,532 --> 01:29:33,368
BLUE TEAM IS OFF TO CATCH EUNSIL

1903
01:29:36,955 --> 01:29:42,544
JANG EUNSIL IS HIDING IN THE SAME SPOT
ON THE SECOND FLOOR OF RED TEAM BASE

1904
01:29:43,420 --> 01:29:44,504
This was the base.

1905
01:29:47,883 --> 01:29:48,967
[Dail] I'll go this way.

1906
01:29:49,634 --> 01:29:50,844
Okay, can you go over there?

1907
01:29:53,513 --> 01:29:57,893
PANI BOTTLE WAS IN RED TEAM BASE

1908
01:30:00,896 --> 01:30:03,189
[♪ tense music playing]

1909
01:30:03,273 --> 01:30:04,524
Yang Dail?

1910
01:30:25,378 --> 01:30:27,589
[Pani Bottle exclaims]
That was a close one.

1911
01:30:27,672 --> 01:30:30,425
HORSEKING IS ONE STEP LATE

1912
01:30:30,508 --> 01:30:32,886
Horseking's that way.
Horseking's at our base.

1913
01:30:32,969 --> 01:30:33,970
[Junseo] Okay.

1914
01:30:34,054 --> 01:30:35,263
[Pani Bottle] Horseking's at our base.

1915
01:30:35,931 --> 01:30:37,474
[Jimin] He said Horseking's at our base.

1916
01:30:38,683 --> 01:30:40,936
[Pani Bottle] Horseking's behind you.
Over there.

1917
01:30:42,771 --> 01:30:44,064
You have to protect us.

1918
01:30:44,147 --> 01:30:45,273
[Jimin] Sure, block Horseking.

1919
01:30:45,774 --> 01:30:46,858
[Ddolddol] I'll stay on Horseking.

1920
01:30:46,942 --> 01:30:48,777
DDOLDDOL IS TRYING
TO PROTECT HIS TEAMMATES

1921
01:30:50,779 --> 01:30:52,030
[Horseking] Where's Eunsil hiding?

1922
01:30:56,493 --> 01:30:57,786
HORSEKING'S SUDDEN CHARGE

1923
01:31:02,582 --> 01:31:04,918
DODGES DDOLDDOL AND TAGS JIMIN

1924
01:31:07,420 --> 01:31:08,797
HORSEKING TAGS PARK JIMIN

1925
01:31:08,880 --> 01:31:10,840
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-[Ddolddol] So tough.

1926
01:31:11,925 --> 01:31:14,511
[Horseking] Our plan
is to take away their cards

1927
01:31:14,594 --> 01:31:15,637
and make them more passive.

1928
01:31:17,889 --> 01:31:19,474
[Jimin panting heavily]

1929
01:31:19,557 --> 01:31:20,642
[Horseking] Where is Eunsil?

1930
01:31:21,142 --> 01:31:24,020
You're not going to play
the King card, right?

1931
01:31:24,104 --> 01:31:25,105
[Horseking] Sorry?

1932
01:31:25,188 --> 01:31:26,898
[Jimin] He's not going to use
the King, right?

1933
01:31:28,400 --> 01:31:30,151
Would he play the King right away?

1934
01:31:31,987 --> 01:31:33,238
[Junseo] Now that
the King's been revealed,

1935
01:31:33,321 --> 01:31:34,948
there's no reason not to play it.

1936
01:31:36,491 --> 01:31:37,617
[groans] Please, use the Joker.

1937
01:31:39,244 --> 01:31:41,371
[Ddolddol] The Joker needs to act
when running and tagging.

1938
01:31:41,454 --> 01:31:42,497
BEFORE START OF GAME

1939
01:31:42,580 --> 01:31:44,708
Then, I'll give you
the Joker to start with.

1940
01:31:44,791 --> 01:31:46,042
-Okay.
-[Ddolddol] Because you're good

1941
01:31:46,126 --> 01:31:47,377
at keeping a poker face.

1942
01:31:47,460 --> 01:31:49,129
-[Pani Bottle] Jimin will take care of it.
-[Ddolddol] Yes.

1943
01:31:49,212 --> 01:31:51,047
[Jimin] I managed to get the Joker.

1944
01:31:51,631 --> 01:31:55,677
THE BATTLE BETWEEN HORSEKING AND JIMIN

1945
01:31:55,760 --> 01:31:57,929
[♪ suspenseful string music playing]

1946
01:32:02,058 --> 01:32:03,643
[scoffs] Seriously.

1947
01:32:04,352 --> 01:32:07,981
[Jimin] If Horseking plays the King
and I play the Joker,

1948
01:32:09,065 --> 01:32:11,484
that would end the game
after only 30 minutes.

1949
01:32:11,568 --> 01:32:15,321
But I think I was unsure
because Horseking had a regular card.

1950
01:32:15,405 --> 01:32:16,781
JOKER LOSES TO ALL CARDS EXCEPT KING

1951
01:32:18,450 --> 01:32:19,451
[exhales deeply]

1952
01:32:19,534 --> 01:32:21,953
[dealer] Mr. Horseking
has submitted his card.

1953
01:32:22,037 --> 01:32:23,496
[Jimin] He wouldn't play the King, right?

1954
01:32:25,665 --> 01:32:27,292
HORSEKING SUBMITS THE KING

1955
01:32:29,085 --> 01:32:30,754
[Horseking] This is all about momentum.

1956
01:32:31,296 --> 01:32:33,882
We need to show
our team's strength from the start.

1957
01:32:35,842 --> 01:32:39,220
[Jimin] Should I play the Joker?
Should I really play it?

1958
01:32:45,393 --> 01:32:47,479
[dealer] Ms. Park Jimin
has submitted her card.

1959
01:32:50,774 --> 01:32:52,275
He wouldn't play the King, right?

1960
01:32:54,569 --> 01:32:57,155
[♪ music crescendos]

1961
01:32:57,238 --> 01:32:58,448
[♪ music fades]

1962
01:32:58,531 --> 01:32:59,783
[dealer] We will announce the results.

1963
01:32:59,866 --> 01:33:01,993
[♪ music continues]

1964
01:33:05,246 --> 01:33:07,248
[♪ ominous music playing]

1965
01:33:27,185 --> 01:33:29,187
Translated by Youji Kim
